{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fk21ykWmAH6tuz5RdBc5kg","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"Classes with `O(n)`-bit layouts? The structural claims of loop0014 item 04\n(`reports/subexp_pathwidth.md` §4), each checked by brute force against\nvertex separation on every graph of the networkx atlas (all graphs to 7\nvertices) before it was stated.\n\n    python -m learning.subexp_classes            # the full check, atlas to 7\n    python -m learning.subexp_classes --nmax 5   # quick\n\nGraphs are `(n, adj)` as in `paper1/complex_check.py`; `vs` is Kinnersley's\nvertex separation (`= pw`), evaluated by the prefix-set DP of\n`learning.subexp_reductions` (itself checked against the permutation minimum\non every atlas graph, §3.5) and, where the claim is about *layouts* rather\nthan values, by `itertools.permutations`.\n\nThe claims:\n\n- **Cobipartite normal form** (§4.1). For `H` with cliques `A`, `B`, some\n  optimal layout places one clique entirely first. With `X` first and `Y` the\n  other side laid out by `τ`, the value is\n  `max(|X| − 1, max_{0 ≤ t < |Y|} (t + |N_X(Y_{>t})|))`, so\n  `vs(H) = min_{X ∈ {A, B}} max(|X| − 1, chain_X)`, where `chain_X` is the\n  minimum over orderings of `Y` — a chain through the one-sided lattice\n  `{S ⊆ Y : |N_X(S)| − |S| ≤ c}`. `cobipartite_normal_form` evaluates it.\n- **Split dichotomy** (§4.2). For a split graph with partition `(K, I)`,\n  `|K| = κ ≥ 1`: `vs ∈ {κ − 1, κ}`, and `vs = κ − 1` iff some `v ∈ K` has\n  a `u ∈ K` adjacent to none of `v`'s independent neighbours.\n  `split_formula` evaluates it.\n- **Twin lemma / unit DP** (§4.5). Twins (`N(x) ∖ {y} = N(y) ∖ {x}`) can be\n  laid out consecutively in some optimal layout, so `vs` is a DP over subsets\n  of twin classes: `O*(2^u)`, `u` the number of classes. `twin_unit_dp`.\n- **Orientations are not certificates** (§4.3): on subcubic graphs the\n  acyclic orientation induced by a layout does not determine the value;\n  `orientation_spread` measures how often its linear extensions disagree.\n- **The gap lemma** (§4.6): the arithmetic of chain certificates at spacing\n  `g` against the two budgets of §1.3.8, `gap_table`.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport itertools\nimport json\nimport math\nimport random\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom functools import lru_cache\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom learning.subexp_reductions import atlas, vs\nfrom paper1.complex_check import graph, vertex_separation, vs_of_layout\n\nOUT = Path(\"reports/scratch/subexp_pathwidth/04_classes\")\nINF = 10 ** 9\n\n\ndef popcount(x: int) -> int:\n    return bin(x).count(\"1\")\n\n\ndef bits(x: int):\n    while x:\n        b = x & -x\n        yield b.bit_length() - 1\n        x ^= b\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# cobipartite graphs\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n====TEST\n\"\"\"loop0014 item 04: the structural claims of `reports/subexp_pathwidth.md` §4\n(cobipartite normal form, split dichotomy, twin lemma) against brute force on\nsmall graphs (the full atlas run is `python -m learning.subexp_classes`).\"\"\"\nimport random\n\nfrom learning import subexp_classes as sc\nfrom learning.subexp_reductions import atlas, vs\nfrom paper1.complex_check import graph\n\n\ndef _graphs(nmax):\n    return atlas(nmax)\n\n\ndef test_cobipartite_normal_form_matches_vs_on_every_partition():\n    for g in _graphs(5):\n        v = vs(g)\n        for A, B in sc.cobipartitions(g):\n            assert sc.cobipartite_normal_form(g, A, B) == v\n\n\ndef test_some_optimal_layout_places_one_clique_first():\n    for g in _graphs(5):\n        v = vs(g)\n        for A, B in sc.cobipartitions(g):\n            assert min(sc.one_side_first_layout_value(g, A, B),\n                       sc.one_side_first_layout_value(g, B, A)) == v\n\n\ndef test_corollary_4_2_decision_on_every_partition_and_k():\n    for g in _graphs(5):\n        v = vs(g)\n        for A, B in sc.cobipartitions(g):\n            for k in range(g[0] + 1):\n                assert sc.cobipartite_decision(g, A, B, k) == (v <= k)\n\n\ndef test_cobipartite_patterns_to_six_vertices():\n    for a in range(1, 4):\n        for b in range(a, 7 - a):\n====LAMPIS\n====BETA\n28:   is `β*(c)` on `G(n, c/n)` and `β*(d, μ)` on random clique covers.\n46:Conversion: the pair exponent's slope at `β*` is `3.3–3.4` per unit of `β`\n55:and on the optimum of random MOSP instances (`β*(c)`, `β*(d, μ)`;\n139:| `c` | `β*` | `β_sep` cited | `β_sep` fitted | `β_closed` | `β_W` (`Ẑ₀`) | best valid | fitted slope | E&M upper | share of the gap closed |\n154:bound on the colourings) is below the closed count everywhere and below `β*`\n155:at `c ≤ 4`. Conversion: the pair exponent's slope at `β*` is `5.5, 3.9, 3.4,\n166:| `(d, μ)` | `β*` | `β_closed` | `β_flip` | best | `b` | E&M upper | share of the gap |\n218:statement about the rare-instance regime at `β*`, where the maximising\n265:| 06 constants | `β_sep − β* < 0.02` at `c = 6, 10` | **met** (`+0.0113`, `+0.0038`); separate: `+0.029` at `c = 3`, threshold `2 ln 2` conditional |\n266:| 07 covers | `β_closed − β* < 0.02` at `(6, 1)`, `(4, 1)` | **met** (`+0.0111`, `+0.0110`); `(8, ½)` at `+0.0211` outside the named cells; zero floor violations on 200 |\n277:  bounds on `lim inf pw/n` under the stated bases; none moves `β*` by `0.02`\n474:| **this repository** | pathwidth; `G(n, c/n)` | empty pairs at exact sizes `t`, `t − 1` | trinomial `C(n, t)C(n − t, t − 1)` | product over edges `(1 − p)^{t(t−1)}` exact | `β*(c)`: 0.0087, 0.061, 0.171, 0.263, 0.337 at `c = 3, 4, 6, 8, 10`; threshold `4 ln 2`; Lean | `random_graph_first_moment.md`; `FirstMoment.lean`, `FirstMomentAsymptotics.lean` |\n475:| this repository | MOSP; random clique covers of given sizes | empty pairs | trinomial | product over patterns of `avoidCount(s)/C(n, s)` exact | `β*(d, μ)`; threshol