{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgiiqdSrfdSonP8aofRJa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"It's 23:03, so I'm aiming to have the report and PROGRESS written by about 02:00. I'm writing the Python module now, covering the independent set, colouring, dominating set, Max-Cut, the Hamiltonian-cycle formula, the model counter, brute-force checks, and the crossover table.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6600,"cache_read_input_tokens":166372,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6600,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2f64960-c328-4d7b-b5d1-fcb61f9722bb","uuid":"381efa40-3fd5-411c-8abd-0e5d0bdb95cf","timestamp":"2026-11-04T23:03:45.836Z","request_id":"req_011CgiiqcjBmseLAARBQMwDx","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":1,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgiiqdSrfdSonP8aofRJa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JZE7n1Z783LG98tZekueod","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/learning/subexp_crossover.py","content":"\"\"\"Algorithms from the counting theorem for problems on graphs of linear\npathwidth: the encodings of loop0014 item 06 (`reports/subexp_pathwidth.md`\n§6), each checked by brute force on every graph of the networkx atlas (all\ngraphs to 7 vertices) before it was stated, and the crossover table.\n\n    python -m learning.subexp_crossover            # the full check, atlas to 7\n    python -m learning.subexp_crossover --nmax 5   # quick\n    python -m learning.subexp_crossover --table    # the crossover table only\n\nGraphs are `(n, adj)` with `adj` a list of neighbour bitmasks, as in\n`paper1/complex_check.py`. A CNF is a list of clauses, each a list of\nnon-zero ints (DIMACS literals); `count_models` is CaDiCaL with a blocking\nclause over every variable (`learning.subexp_chain`), so it counts exactly.\n\nThe encodings, every one with one Boolean variable per vertex (or per edge)\nand auxiliary variables that are *functions* of those, so that the model\ncount is the count of the combinatorial objects (count-preserving):\n\n- `indep_cnf`: independent sets — `¬x_u ∨ ¬x_w` per edge; width 2, `n`\n  variables, `m` clauses; `count = #independent sets` (ETH paper, Cor. 1.3).\n- `indep_atleast_cnf(g, t)`: independent sets of size `≥ t` — the same plus\n  `Σ x_v ≥ t` compiled through a binary adder tree (`popcount_circuit`) and a\n  comparator against the constant `t` (`ge_const`), Tseitin-encoded, width\n  3, `O(n)` auxiliary variables (`THRESHOLD_AUX_PER_INPUT` measured);\n  satisfiable iff `α(G) ≥ t`, `count = #{S independent : |S| ≥ t}`.\n- `coloring_cnf(g, q)`: proper `q`-colourings — `q n` variables, exactly one\n  colour per vertex (one clause of width `q`, `C(q, 2)` of width 2), no\n  equal colours across an edge (`q` clauses of width 2 per edge);\n  `count = #proper q-colourings` (Cor. 1.3).\n- `domset_cnf(g)`: dominating sets — `x_v ∨ ⋁_{u ∈ N(v)} x_u` per vertex,\n  width `Δ + 1`; `domset_cnf(g, tseitin=True)` compiles each clause to width\n  3 with `deg(v)` auxiliaries, so `n + 2m` variables; `domset_atmost_cnf`\n  adds `Σ x_v ≤ t`; satisfiable iff `γ(G) ≤ t`.\n- `maxcut_cnf(g, t)`: one side bit per vertex, one XOR auxiliary per edge,\n  `Σ_e (x_u ⊕ x_w) ≥ t` through the adder tree; `n + O(m)` variables,\n  width 3; satisfiable iff `maxcut(G) ≥ t`, `count = #{sides : cut ≥ t}`.\n- `hamcycle_cutcount_cnf(g)`: Cut & Count with the DP replaced by a count —\n  one variable per edge, one side bit per vertex, exactly two chosen edges\n  at every vertex (two thresholds), a chosen edge keeps both ends on one\n  side, vertex 0 on side 0; `count = Σ_{2-factors X} 2^{cc(X) − 1}`, so\n  `count ≡ #Hamiltonian cycles (mod 2)`. With the isolation lemma's random\n  edge weights (the weighted count, paper form only) the decision follows;\n  `hamcycle_weighted_decision` is that decision by enumeration.\n\n`crossover_table` tabulates `n / (log₂ c · √ln n)` (the paper exponent with\nconstant 1) and `ρ(n) / log₂ c` (the verified exponent, constant 1) for\n`c = 2, 3, 4`: the pathwidth above which `c^{pw}` exceeds the counting bound.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport itertools\nimport json\nimport math\nimport random\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom learning.subexp_chain import count_models\nfrom learning.subexp_reductions import atlas\n\nOUT = Path(\"reports/scratch/subexp_pathwidth/06_crossover\")\n\n\ndef bits(x: int):\n    while x:\n        b = x & -x\n        yield b.bit_length() - 1\n        x ^= b\n\n\ndef popcount(x: int) -> int:\n    return bin(x).count(\"1\")\n\n\ndef edges_of(g):\n    n, adj = g\n    return [(u, w) for u in range(n) for w in bits(adj[u]) if u < w]\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# a Tseitin circuit builder\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass Builder:\n    \"\"\"Clauses over variables `1..nvars`; `fresh()` allocates. `TRUE` is a\n    variable fixed by a unit clause, so constants are determined too and the\n    count is preserved.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, nvars: int = 0):\n        self.nvars = nvars\n        self.clauses: list[list[int]] = []\n        self._true = None\n\n    def fresh(self) -> int:\n        self.nvars += 1\n        return self.nvars\n\n    @property\n    def TRUE(self) -> int:\n        if self._true is None:\n            self._true = self.fresh()\n            self.clauses.append([self._true])\n        return self._true\n\n    @property\n    def FALSE(self) -> int:\n        return -self.TRUE\n\n    def add(self, clause):\n        self.clauses.append(list(clause))\n\n    def xor(self, a: int, b: int) -> int:\n        z = self.fresh()\n        self.add([-a, -b, -z]); self.add([a, b, -z]); self.add([a, -b, z]); self.add([-a, b, z])\n        return z\n\n    def and_(self, a: int, b: int) -> int:\n        z = self.fresh()\n        self.add([-a, -b, z]); self.add([a, -z]); self.add([b, -z])\n        return z\n\n    def or_(self, a: int, b: int) -> int:\n        z = self.fresh()\n        self.add([a, b, -z]); self.add([-a, z]); self.add([-b, z])\n        return z\n\n    def or_many(self, lits) -> int:\n        \"\"\"OR of a list as a chain of binary ORs: `len − 1` auxiliaries.\"\"\"\n        lits = list(lits)\n        if not lits:\n            return self.FALSE\n        acc = lits[0]\n        for l in lits[1:]:\n            acc = self.or_(acc, l)\n        return acc\n\n    def full_adder(self, a: int, b: int, c: int):\n        t = self.xor(a, b)\n        s = self.xor(t, c)\n        carry = self.or_(self.and_(a, b), self.and_(t, c))\n        return s, carry\n\n    def add_numbers(self, A: list[int], B: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Ripple-carry sum of two little-endian bit lists.\"\"\"\n        L = max(len(A), len(B))\n        out, carry = [], None\n        for i in range(L):\n            a = A[i] if i < len(A) else self.FALSE\n            b = B[i] if i < len(B) else self.FALSE\n            if carry is None:\n                s = self.xor(a, b)\n                carry = self.and_(a, b)\n            else:\n                s, carry = self.full_adder(a, b, carry)\n            out.append(s)\n        out.append(carry)\n        return out\n\n    def popcount_circuit(self, lits) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"The binary adder tree: the number of true literals as a\n        little-endian bit list. Total size `O(len)`: level `j` has `len / 2^j`\n        adders of `j + 1` bits.\"\"\"\n        nums = [[l] for l in lits]\n        if not nums:\n            return [self.FALSE]\n        while len(nums) > 1:\n            nxt = [self.add_numbers(nums[i], nums[i + 1]) for i in range(0, len(nums) - 1, 2)]\n            if len(nums) % 2:\n                nxt.append(nums[-1])\n            nums = nxt\n        return nums[0]\n\n    def ge_const(self, num: list[int], t: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"A literal true iff the little-endian number `num` is `≥ t`.\"\"\"\n        L = max(len(num), t.bit_length())\n        ge = self.TRUE\n        for i in range(L):\n            b = num[i] if i < len(num) else self.FALSE\n            ge = self.and_(b, ge) if (t >> i) & 1 else self.or_(b, ge)\n        return ge\n\n    def at_least(self, lits, t: int) -> None:\n        lits = list(lits)\n        if t <= 0:\n            return\n        self.add([self.ge_const(self.popcount_circuit(lits), t)])\n\n    def at_most(self, lits, t: int) -> None:\n        lits = list(lits)\n        self.at_least([-l for l in lits], len(lits) - t)\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# the encodings\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef indep_cnf(g):\n    n, adj = g\n    return [[-(u + 1), -(w + 1)] for u, w in edges_of(g)], n\n\n\ndef indep_atleast_cnf(g, t: int):\n    n, adj = g\n    b = Builder(n)\n    for c, _ in [indep_cnf(g)]:\n        for cl in c:\n            b.add(cl)\n    b.at_least(range(1, n + 1), t)\n    return b.clauses, b.nvars\n\n\ndef coloring_cnf(g, q: int):\n    n, adj = g\n\n    def x(v, c):\n        return v * q + c + 1\n\n    clauses = []\n    for v in range(n):\n        clauses.append([x(v, c) for c in range(q)])\n        for c1 in range(q):\n            for c2 in range(c1 + 1, q):\n                clauses.append([-x(v, c1), -x(v, c2)])\n    for u, w in edges_of(g):\n        for c in range(q):\n            clauses.append([-x(u, c), -x(w, c)])\n    return clauses, n * q\n\n\ndef domset_cnf(g, tseitin: bool = False):\n    n, adj = g\n    if not tseitin:\n        return [[v + 1] + [u + 1 for u in bits(adj[v])] for v in range(n)], n\n    b = Builder(n)\n    for v in range(n):\n        b.add([b.or_many([v + 1] + [u + 1 for u in bits(adj[v])])])\n    return b.clauses, b.nvars\n\n\ndef domset_atmost_cnf(g, t: int):\n    n, adj = g\n    b = Builder(n)\n    for v in range(n):\n        b.add([b.or_many([v + 1] + [u + 1 for u in bits(adj[v])])])\n    b.at_most(range(1, n + 1), t)\n    return b.clauses, b.nvars\n\n\ndef maxcut_cnf(g, t: int):\n    n, adj = g\n    b = Builder(n)\n    cut = [b.xor(u + 1, w + 1) for u, w in edges_of(g)]\n    b.at_least(cut, t)\n    return b.clauses, b.nvars\n\n\ndef hamcycle_cutcount_cnf(g):\n    \"\"\"Variables `1..m` the edges (in `edges_of` order), `m+1..m+n` the sides.\"\"\"\n    n, adj = g\n    E = edges_of(g)\n    m = len(E)\n    b = Builder(m + n)\n    side = [m + v + 1 for v in range(n)]\n    inc = {v: [] for v in range(n)}\n    for i, (u, w) in enumerate(E):\n        inc[u].append(i + 1)\n        inc[w].append(i + 1)\n    for v in range(n):\n        b.at_least(inc[v], 2)\n        b.at_most(inc[v], 2)\n    for i, (u, w) in enumerate(E):\n        e = i + 1\n        b.add([-e, -side[u], side[w]])\n        b.add([-e, side[u], -side[w]])\n    if n:\n        b.add([-side[0]])\n    return b.clauses, b.nvars\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# ground truth, by enumeration that shares nothing with the encodings\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef independent_sets(g):\n    n, adj = g\n    return [S for S in range(1 << n) if all(adj[v] & S == 0 for v in bits(S))]\n\n\ndef dominating_sets(g):\n    n, adj = g\n    full = (1 << n) - 1\n    out = []\n    for S in range(1 << n):\n        N = S\n        for v in bits(S):\n            N |= adj[v]\n        if N == full:\n            out.append(S)\n    return out\n\n\ndef proper_colorings(g, q: int) -> int:\n    n, adj = g\n    E = edges_of(g)\n    return sum(1 for col in itertools.product(range(q), repeat=n)\n               if all(col[u] != col[w] for u, w in E))\n\n\ndef cut_sizes(g):\n    n, adj = g\n    E = edges_of(g)\n    return [sum(1 for u, w in E if (S >> u) & 1 != (S >> w) & 1) for S in range(1 << n)]\n\n\ndef hamiltonian_cycles(g) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Hamiltonian cycles as edge sets: closed tours from vertex 0, divided\n    by 2 (the two directions).\"\"\"\n    n, adj = g\n    if n < 3:\n        return 0\n    cnt = 0\n    for perm in itertools.permutations(range(1, n)):\n        tour = (0,) + perm\n        if all((adj[tour[i]] >> tour[(i + 1) % n]) & 1 for i in range(n)):\n            cnt += 1\n    return cnt // 2\n\n\ndef two_factors(g):\n    \"\"\"Every 2-regular spanning subgraph as an edge subset, with its number\n    of components. Enumerates edge subsets: for `m ≤ 16` only.\"\"\"\n    n, adj = g\n    E = edges_of(g)\n    m = len(E)\n    out = []\n    for X in range(1 << m):\n        deg = [0] * n\n        for i in bits(X):\n            u, w = E[i]\n            deg[u] += 1\n            deg[w] += 1\n        if any(d != 2 for d in deg):\n            continue\n        # components\n        seen, cc = 0, 0\n        nb = [0] * n\n        for i in bits(X):\n            u, w = E[i]\n            nb[u] |= 1 << w\n            nb[w] |= 1 << u\n        for v in range(n):\n            if (seen >> v) & 1:\n                continue\n            cc += 1\n            stack = [v]\n            seen |= 1 << v\n            while stack:\n                a = stack.pop()\n                for c in bits(nb[a] & ~seen):\n                    seen |= 1 << c\n                    stack.append(c)\n        out.append((X, cc))\n    return out\n\n\ndef hamcycle_weighted_decision(g, weights: list[int], limit: int = 10 ** 6):\n    \"\"\"The Cut & Count decision with the given edge weights, by enumerating\n    the models of `hamcycle_cutcount_cnf`: the coefficient of `y^w` in\n    `Σ_X 2^{cc(X) − 1} y^{w(X)}` for each `w`; the answer is \"yes\" iff some\n    coefficient is odd. Sound always; complete with probability `≥ 1/2` under\n    the isolation lemma's weights (Cygan et al. 2011, Lemma 2.1 / Theorem 1).\n    Returns `(decision, coefficients)`.\"\"\"\n    from pysat.solvers import Solver\n    clauses, nvars = hamcycle_cutcount_cnf(g)\n    m = len(edges_of(g))\n    coef: dict[int, int] = {}\n    cnt = 0\n    with Solver(name=\"cadical195\", bootstrap_with=clauses) as s:\n        while s.solve():\n            cnt += 1\n            if cnt > limit:\n                raise RuntimeError(\"model limit\")\n            model = s.get_model()\n            X = [i for i in range(m) if model[i] > 0]\n            w = sum(weights[i] for i in X)\n            coef[w] = coef.get(w, 0) + 1\n            s.add_clause([-l for l in model[:nvars]])\n    return any(c % 2 for c in coef.values()), coef\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# sizes and the crossover table\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef cnf_size(clauses, nvars: int) -> dict:\n    return {\"variables\": nvars, \"clauses\": len(clauses),\n            \"incidence\": sum(len(c) for c in clauses),\n            \"width\": max((len(c) for c in clauses), default=0)}\n\n\ndef threshold_aux_ratio(nmax: int = 200) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Auxiliary variables of `Σ_{i ≤ n} x_i ≥ t` per input, over all `n ≤ nmax`\n    and `t ∈ {1, ⌈n/2⌉, n}`: the constant in `O(n)`.\"\"\"\n    worst = 0.0\n    rows = {}\n    for n in range(1, nmax + 1):\n        for t in {1, (n + 1) // 2, n}:\n            b = Builder(n)\n            b.at_least(range(1, n + 1), t)\n            aux = b.nvars - n\n            worst = max(worst, aux / n)\n            if n in (1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 200) and t == n:\n                rows[n] = {\"aux\": aux, \"clauses\": len(b.clauses), \"width\": max(len(c) for c in b.clauses)}\n    return {\"max_aux_per_input\": worst, \"rows\": rows}\n\n\ndef rho(n: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"The verified runtime scale `n (log log(n + 16))² / √log(n + 16)`.\"\"\"\n    return n * math.log(math.log(n + 16)) ** 2 / math.sqrt(math.log(n + 16))\n\n\ndef crossover_table(cs=(2, 3, 4), exps=(2, 3, 4, 5, 6)) -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"For each `c` and `n = 10^e`: the pathwidth `pw*` with `c^{pw*} = 2^{E(n)}`,\n    `E` the paper exponent `n / √ln n` and the verified `ρ(n)`, both with\n    constant 1; `pw* = E(n) / log₂ c`; and `pw* / n`.\"\"\"\n    rows = []\n    for c in cs:\n        for e in exps:\n            n = 10 ** e\n            paper = n / math.sqrt(math.log(n))\n            ver = rho(n)\n            rows.append({\"c\": c, \"n\": n,\n                         \"paper_exponent\": paper, \"paper_pw_star\": paper / math.log2(c),\n                         \"paper_ratio\": paper / math.log2(c) / n,\n                         \"verified_exponent\": ver, \"verified_pw_star\": ver / math.log2(c),\n                         \"verified_ratio\": ver / math.log2(c) / n})\n    return rows\n\n\ndef format_table(rows) -> str:\n    lines = [\"| c | n | paper: pw* = n/(log₂c √ln n) | pw*/n | verified: pw* = ρ(n)/log₂c | pw*/n |\",\n             \"|---|---|---|---|---|---|\"]\n    for r in rows:\n        lines.append(f\"| {r['c']} | 10^{int(math.log10(r['n']))} | {r['paper_pw_star']:,.0f} | \"\n                     f\"{r['paper_ratio']:.3f} | {r['verified_pw_star']:,.0f} | {r['verified_ratio']:.3f} |\")\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# the checks\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef run_checks(nmax: int = 7, out_dir: Path = OUT, log=print, qs=(2, 3), q4_nmax: int = 6,\n               twofactor_mmax: int = 15, seed: int = 0) -> dict:\n    out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\n    t0 = time.time()\n    graphs = atlas(nmax)\n    log(f\"atlas to {nmax} vertices: {len(graphs)} graphs\")\n    res = {\"nmax\": nmax, \"graphs\": len(graphs), \"failures\": [], \"checks\": {}}\n    fails = res[\"failures\"]\n    C = {k: 0 for k in [\"indep_count\", \"indep_width\", \"indep_size\",\n                        \"indep_atleast_count\", \"indep_atleast_sat\", \"indep_atleast_width\",\n                        \"coloring_count\", \"coloring_width\", \"coloring_size\",\n                        \"domset_count\", \"domset_width\", \"domset_tseitin_count\", \"domset_tseitin_width\",\n                        \"domset_atmost_sat\", \"maxcut_sat\", \"maxcut_count\", \"maxcut_width\",\n                        \"ham_parity\", \"ham_count_2factors\", \"ham_weighted_sound\", \"ham_width\",\n                        \"ham_size\"]}\n    sizes = {\"indep\": [], \"indep_atleast\": [], \"coloring3\": [], \"domset_tseitin\": [], \"maxcut\": [], \"ham\": []}\n    ham_complete = [0, 0]\n    for gi, g in enumerate(graphs):\n        n, adj = g\n        E = edges_of(g)\n        m = len(E)\n\n        # independent sets\n        cl, nv = indep_cnf(g)\n        IS = independent_sets(g)\n        sz = cnf_size(cl, nv)\n        if count_models(cl, nv) != len(IS):\n            fails.append((\"indep_count\", gi))\n        C[\"indep_count\"] += 1\n        if sz[\"width\"] > 2:\n            fails.append((\"indep_width\", gi))\n        C[\"indep_width\"] += 1\n        if not (nv == n and sz[\"clauses\"] == m):\n            fails.append((\"indep_size\", gi))\n        C[\"indep_size\"] += 1\n        sizes[\"indep\"].append((n, m, nv, sz[\"clauses\"]))\n        alpha = max(popcount(S) for S in IS)\n        for t in range(n + 2):\n            cl, nv = indep_atleast_cnf(g, t)\n            cnt = count_models(cl, nv)\n            if cnt != sum(1 for S in IS if popcount(S) >= t):\n                fails.append((\"indep_atleast_count\", gi, t))\n            C[\"indep_atleast_count\"] += 1\n            if (cnt > 0) != (alpha >= t):\n                fails.append((\"indep_atleast_sat\", gi, t))\n            C[\"indep_atleast_sat\"] += 1\n            sz = cnf_size(cl, nv)\n            if sz[\"width\"] > 3:\n                fails.append((\"indep_atleast_width\", gi, t))\n            C[\"indep_atleast_width\"] += 1\n            if t == (n + 1) // 2:\n                sizes[\"indep_atleast\"].append((n, m, nv, sz[\"clauses\"]))\n\n        # colourings\n        for q in list(qs) + ([4] if n <= q4_nmax else []):\n            cl, nv = coloring_cnf(g, q)\n            if count_models(cl, nv) != proper_colorings(g, q):\n                fails.append((\"coloring_count\", gi, q))\n            C[\"coloring_count\"] += 1\n            sz = cnf_size(cl, nv)\n            if sz[\"width\"] > max(q, 2):\n                fails.append((\"coloring_width\", gi, q))\n            C[\"coloring_width\"] += 1\n            if not (nv == n * q and sz[\"clauses\"] == n + n * q * (q - 1) // 2 + q * m):\n                fails.append((\"coloring_size\", gi, q))\n            C[\"coloring_size\"] += 1\n            if q == 3:\n                sizes[\"coloring3\"].append((n, m, nv, sz[\"clauses\"]))\n\n        # dominating sets\n        DS = dominating_sets(g)\n        gamma = min(popcount(S) for S in DS)\n        Delta = max((popcount(a) for a in adj), default=0)\n        cl, nv = domset_cnf(g)\n        if count_models(cl, nv) != len(DS):\n            fails.append((\"domset_count\", gi))\n        C[\"domset_count\"] += 1\n        if cnf_size(cl, nv)[\"width\"] != Delta + 1:\n            fails.append((\"domset_width\", gi))\n        C[\"domset_width\"] += 1\n        cl, nv = domset_cnf(g, tseitin=True)\n        if count_models(cl, nv) != len(DS):\n            fails.append((\"domset_tseitin_count\", gi))\n        C[\"domset_tseitin_count\"] += 1\n        sz = cnf_size(cl, nv)\n        if sz[\"width\"] > 3 or nv > n + 2 * m + 1:\n            fails.append((\"domset_tseitin_width\", gi))\n        C[\"domset_tseitin_width\"] += 1\n        sizes[\"domset_tseitin\"].append((n, m, nv, sz[\"clauses\"]))\n        for t in range(n + 1):\n            cl, nv = domset_atmost_cnf(g, t)\n            if (count_models(cl, nv) > 0) != (gamma <= t):\n                fails.append((\"domset_atmost_sat\", gi, t))\n            C[\"domset_atmost_sat\"] += 1\n\n        # max cut\n        cuts = cut_sizes(g)\n        mc = max(cuts)\n        for t in range(m + 2):\n            cl, nv = maxcut_cnf(g, t)\n            cnt = count_models(cl, nv)\n            if (cnt > 0) != (mc >= t):\n                fails.append((\"maxcut_sat\", gi, t))\n            C[\"maxcut_sat\"] += 1\n            if cnt != sum(1 for c in cuts if c >= t):\n                fails.append((\"maxcut_count\", gi, t))\n            C[\"maxcut_count\"] += 1\n            sz = cnf_size(cl, nv)\n            if sz[\"width\"] > 3:\n                fails.append((\"maxcut_width\", gi, t))\n            C[\"maxcut_width\"] += 1\n            if t == (m + 1) // 2:\n                sizes[\"maxcut\"].append((n, m, nv, sz[\"clauses\"]))\n\n        # Hamiltonian cycles: Cut & Count as a count\n        if n >= 3:\n            cl, nv = hamcycle_cutcount_cnf(g)\n            cnt = count_models(cl, nv)\n            hc = hamiltonian_cycles(g)\n            if cnt % 2 != hc % 2:\n                fails.append((\"ham_parity\", gi))\n            C[\"ham_parity\"] += 1\n            sz = cnf_size(cl, nv)\n            if sz[\"width\"] > 3:\n                fails.append((\"ham_width\", gi))\n            C[\"ham_width\"] += 1\n            if nv > m + n + 40 * (2 * m) + 1:\n                fails.append((\"ham_size\", gi))\n            C[\"ham_size\"] += 1\n            sizes[\"ham\"].append((n, m, nv, sz[\"clauses\"]))\n            if m <= twofactor_mmax:\n                tf = two_factors(g)\n                if cnt != sum(2 ** (cc - 1) for _, cc in tf):\n                    fails.append((\"ham_count_2factors\", gi))\n                C[\"ham_count_2factors\"] += 1\n            weights = [rng.randint(1, 2 * m) for _ in range(m)]\n            dec, _ = hamcycle_weighted_decision(g, weights)\n            if dec and hc == 0:\n                fails.append((\"ham_weighted_sound\", gi))\n            C[\"ham_weighted_sound\"] += 1\n            if hc > 0:\n                ham_complete[1] += 1\n                ham_complete[0] += int(dec)\n\n        if (gi + 1) % 200 == 0:\n            log(f\"  {gi + 1}/{len(graphs)} graphs, {len(fails)} failures, {time.time() - t0:.1f} s\")\n\n    res[\"checks\"] = C\n    res[\"ham_weighted_complete\"] = {\"decided_yes\": ham_complete[0], \"with_cycle\": ham_complete[1]}\n    # linear size bounds, as measured constants\n    lin = {}\n    for key, rows in sizes.items():\n        if rows:\n            lin[key] = {\"max_vars_over_n_plus_m\": max(v / (n + m) for n, m, v, c in rows),\n                        \"max_clauses_over_n_plus_m\": max(c / (n + m) for n, m, v, c in rows)}\n    res[\"size_constants\"] = lin\n    res[\"threshold_aux\"] = threshold_aux_ratio()\n    res[\"crossover_table\"] = crossover_table()\n    res[\"seconds\"] = time.time() - t0\n    log(f\"checks: {sum(C.values())} evaluations, {len(fails)} failures, {res['seconds']:.1f} s\")\n    for k, v in C.items():\n        log(f\"  {k}: {v}\")\n    log(f\"Cut & Count weighted decision: yes on {ham_complete[0]} of {ham_complete[1]} graphs with a cycle\"\n        f\" (sound on all: {C['ham_weighted_sound']} checked)\")\n    log(\"size constants: \" + json.dumps(lin))\n    log(f\"threshold auxiliaries per input, n ≤ 200: ≤ {res['threshold_aux']['max_aux_per_input']:.2f}\")\n    log(format_table(res[\"crossover_table\"]))\n    if fails:\n        log(\"FAILURES: \" + str(fails[:20]))\n    (out_dir / \"check.json\").write_text(json.dumps(res, indent=1, default=str))\n    return res\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"--nmax\", type=int, default=7)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--table\", action=\"store_true\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out\", type=Path, default=OUT)\n    a = ap.parse_args()\n    if a.table:\n        print(format_table(crossover_table()))\n        return\n    res = run_checks(a.nmax, a.out)\n    sys.exit(1 if res[\"failures\"] else 0)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6600,"cache_read_input_tokens":166372,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6600,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2f64960-c328-4d7b-b5d1-fcb61f9722bb","uuid":"b5ebc665-e62a-47fa-9731-498783813677","timestamp":"2026-11-04T23:05:24.149Z","request_id":"req_011CgiiqcjBmseLAARBQMwDx","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01JZE7n1Z783LG98tZekueod":{"file_path":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/learning/subexp_crossover.py","content":"\"\"\"Algorithms from the counting theorem for problems on graphs of linear\npathwidth: the encodings of loop0014 item 06 (`reports/subexp_pathwidth.md`\n§6), each checked by brute force on every graph of the networkx atlas (all\ngraphs to 7 vertices) before it was stated, and the crossover table.\n\n    python -m learning.subexp_crossover            # the full check, atlas to 7\n    python -m learning.subexp_crossover --nmax 5   # quick\n    python -m learning.subexp_crossover --table    # the crossover table only\n\nGraphs are `(n, adj)` with `adj` a list of neighbour bitmasks, as in\n`paper1/complex_check.py`. A CNF is a list of clauses, each a list of\nnon-zero ints (DIMACS literals); `count_models` is CaDiCaL with a blocking\nclause over every variable (`learning.subexp_chain`), so it counts exactly.\n\nThe encodings, every one with one Boolean variable per vertex (or per edge)\nand auxiliary variables that are *functions* of those, so that the model\ncount is the count of the combinatorial objects (count-preserving):\n\n- `indep_cnf`: independent sets — `¬x_u ∨ ¬x_w` per edge; width 2, `n`\n  variables, `m` clauses; `count = #independent sets` (ETH paper, Cor. 1.3).\n- `indep_atleast_cnf(g, t)`: independent sets of size `≥ t` — the same plus\n  `Σ x_v ≥ t` compiled through a binary adder tree (`popcount_circuit`) and a\n  comparator against the constant `t` (`ge_const`), Tseitin-encoded, width\n  3, `O(n)` auxiliary variables (`THRESHOLD_AUX_PER_INPUT` measured);\n  satisfiable iff `α(G) ≥ t`, `count = #{S independent : |S| ≥ t}`.\n- `coloring_cnf(g, q)`: proper `q`-colourings — `q n` variables, exactly one\n  colour per vertex (one clause of width `q`, `C(q, 2)` of width 2), no\n  equal colours across an edge (`q` clauses of width 2 per edge);\n  `count = #proper q-colourings` (Cor. 1.3).\n- `domset_cnf(g)`: dominating sets — `x_v ∨ ⋁_{u ∈ N(v)} x_u` per vertex,\n  width `Δ + 1`; `domset_cnf(g, tseitin=True)` compiles each clause to width\n  3 with `deg(v)` auxiliaries, so `n + 2m` variables; `domset_atmost_cnf`\n  adds `Σ x_v ≤ t`; satisfiable iff `γ(G) ≤ t`.\n- `maxcut_cnf(g, t)`: one side bit per vertex, one XOR auxiliary per edge,\n  `Σ_e (x_u ⊕ x_w) ≥ t` through the adder tree; `n + O(m)` variables,\n  width 3; satisfiable iff `maxcut(G) ≥ t`, `count = #{sides : cut ≥ t}`.\n- `hamcycle_cutcount_cnf(g)`: Cut & Count with the DP replaced by a count —\n  one variable per edge, one side bit per vertex, exactly two chosen edges\n  at every vertex (two thresholds), a chosen edge keeps both ends on one\n  side, vertex 0 on side 0; `count = Σ_{2-factors X} 2^{cc(X) − 1}`, so\n  `count ≡ #Hamiltonian cycles (mod 2)`. With the isolation lemma's random\n  edge weights (the weighted count, paper form only) the decision follows;\n  `hamcycle_weighted_decision` is that decision by enumeration.\n\n`crossover_table` tabulates `n / (log₂ c · √ln n)` (the paper exponent with\nconstant 1) and `ρ(n) / log₂ c` (the verified exponent, constant 1) for\n`c = 2, 3, 4`: the pathwidth above which `c^{pw}` exceeds the counting bound.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport itertools\nimport json\nimport math\nimport random\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom learning.subexp_chain import count_models\nfrom learning.subexp_reductions import atlas\n\nOUT = Path(\"reports/scratch/subexp_pathwidth/06_crossover\")\n\n\ndef bits(x: int):\n    while x:\n        b = x & -x\n        yield b.bit_length() - 1\n        x ^= b\n\n\ndef popcount(x: int) -> int:\n    return bin(x).count(\"1\")\n\n\ndef edges_of(g):\n    n, adj = g\n    return [(u, w) for u in range(n) for w in bits(adj[u]) if u < w]\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# a Tseitin circuit builder\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass Builder:\n    \"\"\"Clauses over variables `1..nvars`; `fresh()` allocates. `TRUE` is a\n    variable fixed by a unit clause, so constants are determined too and the\n    count is preserved.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, nvars: int = 0):\n        self.nvars = nvars\n        self.clauses: list[list[int]] = []\n        self._true = None\n\n    def fresh(self) -> int:\n        self.nvars += 1\n        return self.nvars\n\n    @property\n    def TRUE(self) -> int:\n        if self._true is None:\n            self._true = self.fresh()\n            self.clauses.append([self._true])\n        return self._true\n\n    @property\n    def FALSE(self) -> int:\n        return -self.TRUE\n\n    def add(self, clause):\n        self.clauses.append(list(clause))\n\n    def xor(self, a: int, b: int) -> int:\n        z = self.fresh()\n        self.add([-a, -b, -z]); self.add([a, b, -z]); self.add([a, -b, z]); self.add([-a, b, z])\n        return z\n\n    def and_(self, a: int, b: int) -> int:\n        z = self.fresh()\n        self.add([-a, -b, z]); self.add([a, -z]); self.add([b, -z])\n        return z\n\n    def or_(self, a: int, b: int) -> int:\n        z = self.fresh()\n        self.add([a, b, -z]); self.add([-a, z]); self.add([-b, z])\n        return z\n\n    def or_many(self, lits) -> int:\n        \"\"\"OR of a list as a chain of binary ORs: `len − 1` auxiliaries.\"\"\"\n        lits = list(lits)\n        if not lits:\n            return self.FALSE\n        acc = lits[0]\n        for l in lits[1:]:\n            acc = self.or_(acc, l)\n        return acc\n\n    def full_adder(self, a: int, b: int, c: int):\n        t = self.xor(a, b)\n        s = self.xor(t, c)\n        carry = self.or_(self.and_(a, b), self.and_(t, c))\n        return s, carry\n\n    def add_numbers(self, A: list[int], B: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Ripple-carry sum of two little-endian bit lists.\"\"\"\n        L = max(len(A), len(B))\n        out, carry = [], None\n        for i in range(L):\n            a = A[i] if i < len(A) else self.FALSE\n            b = B[i] if i < len(B) else self.FALSE\n            if carry is None:\n                s = self.xor(a, b)\n                carry = self.and_(a, b)\n            else:\n                s, carry = self.full_adder(a, b, carry)\n            out.append(s)\n        out.append(carry)\n        return out\n\n    def popcount_circuit(self, lits) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"The binary adder tree: the number of true literals as a\n        little-endian bit list. Total size `O(len)`: level `j` has `len / 2^j`\n        adders of `j + 1` bits.\"\"\"\n        nums = [[l] for l in lits]\n        if not nums:\n            return [self.FALSE]\n        while len(nums) > 1:\n            nxt = [self.add_numbers(nums[i], nums[i + 1]) for i in range(0, len(nums) - 1, 2)]\n            if len(nums) % 2:\n                nxt.append(nums[-1])\n            nums = nxt\n        return nums[0]\n\n    def ge_const(self, num: list[int], t: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"A literal true iff the little-endian number `num` is `≥ t`.\"\"\"\n        L = max(len(num), t.bit_length())\n        ge = self.TRUE\n        for i in range(L):\n            b = num[i] if i < len(num) else self.FALSE\n            ge = self.and_(b, ge) if (t >> i) & 1 else self.or_(b, ge)\n        return ge\n\n    def at_least(self, lits, t: int) -> None:\n        lits = list(lits)\n        if t <= 0:\n            return\n        self.add([self.ge_const(self.popcount_circuit(lits), t)])\n\n    def at_most(self, lits, t: int) -> None:\n        lits = list(lits)\n        self.at_least([-l for l in lits], len(lits) - t)\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# the encodings\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef indep_cnf(g):\n    n, adj = g\n    return [[-(u + 1), -(w + 1)] for u, w in edges_of(g)], n\n\n\ndef indep_atleast_cnf(g, t: int):\n    n, adj = g\n    b = Builder(n)\n    for c, _ in [indep_cnf(g)]:\n        for cl in c:\n            b.add(cl)\n    b.at_least(range(1, n + 1), t)\n    return b.clauses, b.nvars\n\n\ndef coloring_cnf(g, q: int):\n    n, adj = g\n\n    def x(v, c):\n        return v * q + c + 1\n\n    clauses = []\n    for v in range(n):\n        clauses.append([x(v, c) for c in range(q)])\n        for c1 in range(q):\n            for c2 in range(c1 + 1, q):\n                clauses.append([-x(v, c1), -x(v, c2)])\n    for u, w in edges_of(g):\n        for c in range(q):\n            clauses.append([-x(u, c), -x(w, c)])\n    return clauses, n * q\n\n\ndef domset_cnf(g, tseitin: bool = False):\n    n, adj = g\n    if not tseitin:\n        return [[v + 1] + [u + 1 for u in bits(adj[v])] for v in range(n)], n\n    b = Builder(n)\n    for v in range(n):\n        b.add([b.or_many([v + 1] + [u + 1 for u in bits(adj[v])])])\n    return b.clauses, b.nvars\n\n\ndef domset_atmost_cnf(g, t: int):\n    n, adj = g\n    b = Builder(n)\n    for v in range(n):\n        b.add([b.or_many([v + 1] + [u + 1 for u in bits(adj[v])])])\n    b.at_most(range(1, n + 1), t)\n    return b.clauses, b.nvars\n\n\ndef maxcut_cnf(g, t: int):\n    n, adj = g\n    b = Builder(n)\n    cut = [b.xor(u + 1, w + 1) for u, w in edges_of(g)]\n    b.at_least(cut, t)\n    return b.clauses, b.nvars\n\n\ndef hamcycle_cutcount_cnf(g):\n    \"\"\"Variables `1..m` the edges (in `edges_of` order), `m+1..m+n` the sides.\"\"\"\n    n, adj = g\n    E = edges_of(g)\n    m = len(E)\n    b = Builder(m + n)\n    side = [m + v + 1 for v in range(n)]\n    inc = {v: [] for v in range(n)}\n    for i, (u, w) in enumerate(E):\n        inc[u].append(i + 1)\n        inc[w].append(i + 1)\n    for v in range(n):\n        b.at_least(inc[v], 2)\n        b.at_most(inc[v], 2)\n    for i, (u, w) in enumerate(E):\n        e = i + 1\n        b.add([-e, -side[u], side[w]])\n        b.add([-e, side[u], -side[w]])\n    if n:\n        b.add([-side[0]])\n    return b.clauses, b.nvars\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# ground truth, by enumeration that shares nothing with the encodings\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef independent_sets(g):\n    n, adj = g\n    return [S for S in range(1 << n) if all(adj[v] & S == 0 for v in bits(S))]\n\n\ndef dominating_sets(g):\n    n, adj = g\n    full = (1 << n) - 1\n    out = []\n    for S in range(1 << n):\n        N = S\n        for v in bits(S):\n            N |= adj[v]\n        if N == full:\n            out.append(S)\n    return out\n\n\ndef proper_colorings(g, q: int) -> int:\n    n, adj = g\n    E = edges_of(g)\n    return sum(1 for col in itertools.product(range(q), repeat=n)\n               if all(col[u] != col[w] for u, w in E))\n\n\ndef cut_sizes(g):\n    n, adj = g\n    E = edges_of(g)\n    return [sum(1 for u, w in E if (S >> u) & 1 != (S >> w) & 1) for S in range(1 << n)]\n\n\ndef hamiltonian_cycles(g) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Hamiltonian cycles as edge sets: closed tours from vertex 0, divided\n    by 2 (the two directions).\"\"\"\n    n, adj = g\n    if n < 3:\n        return 0\n    cnt = 0\n    for perm in itertools.permutations(range(1, n)):\n        tour = (0,) + perm\n        if all((adj[tour[i]] >> tour[(i + 1) % n]) & 1 for i in range(n)):\n            cnt += 1\n    return cnt // 2\n\n\ndef two_factors(g):\n    \"\"\"Every 2-regular spanning subgraph as an edge subset, with its number\n    of components. Enumerates edge subsets: for `m ≤ 16` only.\"\"\"\n    n, adj = g\n    E = edges_of(g)\n    m = len(E)\n    out = []\n    for X in range(1 << m):\n        deg = [0] * n\n        for i in bits(X):\n            u, w = E[i]\n            deg[u] += 1\n            deg[w] += 1\n        if any(d != 2 for d in deg):\n            continue\n        # components\n        seen, cc = 0, 0\n        nb = [0] * n\n        for i in bits(X):\n            u, w = E[i]\n            nb[u] |= 1 << w\n            nb[w] |= 1 << u\n        for v in range(n):\n            if (seen >> v) & 1:\n                continue\n            cc += 1\n            stack = [v]\n            seen |= 1 << v\n            while stack:\n                a = stack.pop()\n                for c in bits(nb[a] & ~seen):\n                    seen |= 1 << c\n                    stack.append(c)\n        out.append((X, cc))\n    return out\n\n\ndef hamcycle_weighted_decision(g, weights: list[int], limit: int = 10 ** 6):\n    \"\"\"The Cut & Count decision with the given edge weights, by enumerating\n    the models of `hamcycle_cutcount_cnf`: the coefficient of `y^w` in\n    `Σ_X 2^{cc(X) − 1} y^{w(X)}` for each `w`; the answer is \"yes\" iff some\n    coefficient is odd. Sound always; complete with probability `≥ 1/2` under\n    the isolation lemma's weights (Cygan et al. 2011, Lemma 2.1 / Theorem 1).\n    Returns `(decision, coefficients)`.\"\"\"\n    from pysat.solvers import Solver\n    clauses, nvars = hamcycle_cutcount_cnf(g)\n    m = len(edges_of(g))\n    coef: dict[int, int] = {}\n    cnt = 0\n    with Solver(name=\"cadical195\", bootstrap_with=clauses) as s:\n        while s.solve():\n            cnt += 1\n            if cnt > limit:\n                raise RuntimeError(\"model limit\")\n            model = s.get_model()\n            X = [i for i in range(m) if model[i] > 0]\n            w = sum(weights[i] for i in X)\n            coef[w] = coef.get(w, 0) + 1\n            s.add_clause([-l for l in model[:nvars]])\n    return any(c % 2 for c in coef.values()), coef\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# sizes and the crossover table\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef cnf_size(clauses, nvars: int) -> dict:\n    return {\"variables\": nvars, \"clauses\": len(clauses),\n            \"incidence\": sum(len(c) for c in clauses),\n            \"width\": max((len(c) for c in clauses), default=0)}\n\n\ndef threshold_aux_ratio(nmax: int = 200) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Auxiliary variables of `Σ_{i ≤ n} x_i ≥ t` per input, over all `n ≤ nmax`\n    and `t ∈ {1, ⌈n/2⌉, n}`: the constant in `O(n)`.\"\"\"\n    worst = 0.0\n    rows = {}\n    for n in range(1, nmax + 1):\n        for t in {1, (n + 1) // 2, n}:\n            b = Builder(n)\n            b.at_least(range(1, n + 1), t)\n            aux = b.nvars - n\n            worst = max(worst, aux / n)\n            if n in (1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 200) and t == n:\n                rows[n] = {\"aux\": aux, \"clauses\": len(b.clauses), \"width\": max(len(c) for c in b.clauses)}\n    return {\"max_aux_per_input\": worst, \"rows\": rows}\n\n\ndef rho(n: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"The verified runtime scale `n (log log(n + 16))² / √log(n + 16)`.\"\"\"\n    return n * math.log(math.log(n + 16)) ** 2 / math.sqrt(math.log(n + 16))\n\n\ndef crossover_table(cs=(2, 3, 4), exps=(2, 3, 4, 5, 6)) -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"For each `c` and `n = 10^e`: the pathwidth `pw*` with `c^{pw*} = 2^{E(n)}`,\n    `E` the paper exponent `n / √ln n` and the verified `ρ(n)`, both with\n    constant 1; `pw* = E(n) / log₂ c`; and `pw* / n`.\"\"\"\n    rows = []\n    for c in cs:\n        for e in exps:\n            n = 10 ** e\n            paper = n / math.sqrt(math.log(n))\n            ver = rho(n)\n            rows.append({\"c\": c, \"n\": n,\n                         \"paper_exponent\": paper, \"paper_pw_star\": paper / math.log2(c),\n                         \"paper_ratio\": paper / math.log2(c) / n,\n                         \"verified_exponent\": ver, \"verified_pw_star\": ver / math.log2(c),\n                         \"verified_ratio\": ver / math.log2(c) / n})\n    return rows\n\n\ndef format_table(rows) -> str:\n    lines = [\"| c | n | paper: pw* = n/(log₂c √ln n) | pw*/n | verified: pw* = ρ(n)/log₂c | pw*/n |\",\n             \"|---|---|---|---|---|---|\"]\n    for r in rows:\n        lines.append(f\"| {r['c']} | 10^{int(math.log10(r['n']))} | {r['paper_pw_star']:,.0f} | \"\n                     f\"{r['paper_ratio']:.3f} | {r['verified_pw_star']:,.0f} | {r['verified_ratio']:.3f} |\")\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# the checks\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef run_checks(nmax: int = 7, out_dir: Path = OUT, log=print, qs=(2, 3), q4_nmax: int = 6,\n               twofactor_mmax: int = 15, seed: int = 0) -> dict:\n    out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\n    t0 = time.time()\n    graphs = atlas(nmax)\n    log(f\"atlas to {nmax} vertices: {len(graphs)} graphs\")\n    res = {\"nmax\": nmax, \"graphs\": len(graphs), \"failures\": [], \"checks\": {}}\n    fails = res[\"failures\"]\n    C = {k: 0 for k in [\"indep_count\", \"indep_width\", \"indep_size\",\n                        \"indep_atleast_count\", \"indep_atleast_sat\", \"indep_atleast_width\",\n                        \"coloring_count\", \"coloring_width\", \"coloring_size\",\n                        \"domset_count\", \"domset_width\", \"domset_tseitin_count\", \"domset_tseitin_width\",\n                        \"domset_atmost_sat\", \"maxcut_sat\", \"maxcut_count\", \"maxcut_width\",\n                        \"ham_parity\", \"ham_count_2factors\", \"ham_weighted_sound\", \"ham_width\",\n                        \"ham_size\"]}\n    sizes = {\"indep\": [], \"indep_atleast\": [], \"coloring3\": [], \"domset_tseitin\": [], \"maxcut\": [], \"ham\": []}\n    ham_complete = [0, 0]\n    for gi, g in enumerate(graphs):\n        n, adj = g\n        E = edges_of(g)\n        m = len(E)\n\n        # independent sets\n        cl, nv = indep_cnf(g)\n        IS = independent_sets(g)\n        sz = cnf_size(cl, nv)\n        if count_models(cl, nv) != len(IS):\n            fails.append((\"indep_count\", gi))\n        C[\"indep_count\"] += 1\n        if sz[\"width\"] > 2:\n            fails.append((\"indep_width\", gi))\n        C[\"indep_width\"] += 1\n        if not (nv == n and sz[\"clauses\"] == m):\n            fails.append((\"indep_size\", gi))\n        C[\"indep_size\"] += 1\n        sizes[\"indep\"].append((n, m, nv, sz[\"clauses\"]))\n        alpha = max(popcount(S) for S in IS)\n        for t in range(n + 2):\n            cl, nv = indep_atleast_cnf(g, t)\n            cnt = count_models(cl, nv)\n            if cnt != sum(1 for S in IS if popcount(S) >= t):\n                fails.append((\"indep_atleast_count\", gi, t))\n            C[\"indep_atleast_count\"] += 1\n            if (cnt > 0) != (alpha >= t):\n                fails.append((\"indep_atleast_sat\", gi, t))\n            C[\"indep_atleast_sat\"] += 1\n            sz = cnf_size(cl, nv)\n            if sz[\"width\"] > 3:\n                fails.append((\"indep_atleast_width\", gi, t))\n            C[\"indep_atleast_width\"] += 1\n            if t == (n + 1) // 2:\n                sizes[\"indep_atleast\"].append((n, m, nv, sz[\"clauses\"]))\n\n        # colourings\n        for q in list(qs) + ([4] if n <= q4_nmax else []):\n            cl, nv = coloring_cnf(g, q)\n            if count_models(cl, nv) != proper_colorings(g, q):\n                fails.append((\"coloring_count\", gi, q))\n            C[\"coloring_count\"] += 1\n            sz = cnf_size(cl, nv)\n            if sz[\"width\"] > max(q, 2):\n                fails.append((\"coloring_width\", gi, q))\n            C[\"coloring_width\"] += 1\n            if not (nv == n * q and sz[\"clauses\"] == n + n * q * (q - 1) // 2 + q * m):\n                fails.append((\"coloring_size\", gi, q))\n            C[\"coloring_size\"] += 1\n            if q == 3:\n                sizes[\"coloring3\"].append((n, m, nv, sz[\"clauses\"]))\n\n        # dominating sets\n        DS = dominating_sets(g)\n        gamma = min(popcount(S) for S in DS)\n        Delta = max((popcount(a) for a in adj), default=0)\n        cl, nv = domset_cnf(g)\n        if count_models(cl, nv) != len(DS):\n            fails.append((\"domset_count\", gi))\n        C[\"domset_count\"] += 1\n        if cnf_size(cl, nv)[\"width\"] != Delta + 1:\n            fails.append((\"domset_width\", gi))\n        C[\"domset_width\"] += 1\n        cl, nv = domset_cnf(g, tseitin=True)\n        if count_models(cl, nv) != len(DS):\n            fails.append((\"domset_tseitin_count\", gi))\n        C[\"domset_tseitin_count\"] += 1\n        sz = cnf_size(cl, nv)\n        if sz[\"width\"] > 3 or nv > n + 2 * m + 1:\n            fails.append((\"domset_tseitin_width\", gi))\n        C[\"domset_tseitin_width\"] += 1\n        sizes[\"domset_tseitin\"].append((n, m, nv, sz[\"clauses\"]))\n        for t in range(n + 1):\n            cl, nv = domset_atmost_cnf(g, t)\n            if (count_models(cl, nv) > 0) != (gamma <= t):\n                fails.append((\"domset_atmost_sat\", gi, t))\n            C[\"domset_atmost_sat\"] += 1\n\n        # max cut\n        cuts = cut_sizes(g)\n        mc = max(cuts)\n        for t in range(m + 2):\n            cl, nv = maxcut_cnf(g, t)\n            cnt = count_models(cl, nv)\n            if (cnt > 0) != (mc >= t):\n                fails.append((\"maxcut_sat\", gi, t))\n            C[\"maxcut_sat\"] += 1\n            if cnt != sum(1 for c in cuts if c >= t):\n                fails.append((\"maxcut_count\", gi, t))\n            C[\"maxcut_count\"] += 1\n            sz = cnf_size(cl, nv)\n            if sz[\"width\"] > 3:\n                fails.append((\"maxcut_width\", gi, t))\n            C[\"maxcut_width\"] += 1\n            if t == (m + 1) // 2:\n                sizes[\"maxcut\"].append((n, m, nv, sz[\"clauses\"]))\n\n        # Hamiltonian cycles: Cut & Count as a count\n        if n >= 3:\n            cl, nv = hamcycle_cutcount_cnf(g)\n            cnt = count_models(cl, nv)\n            hc = hamiltonian_cycles(g)\n            if cnt % 2 != hc % 2:\n                fails.append((\"ham_parity\", gi))\n            C[\"ham_parity\"] += 1\n            sz = cnf_size(cl, nv)\n            if sz[\"width\"] > 3:\n                fails.append((\"ham_width\", gi))\n            C[\"ham_width\"] += 1\n            if nv > m + n + 40 * (2 * m) + 1:\n                fails.append((\"ham_size\", gi))\n            C[\"ham_size\"] += 1\n            sizes[\"ham\"].append((n, m, nv, sz[\"clauses\"]))\n            if m <= twofactor_mmax:\n                tf = two_factors(g)\n                if cnt != sum(2 ** (cc - 1) for _, cc in tf):\n                    fails.append((\"ham_count_2factors\", gi))\n                C[\"ham_count_2factors\"] += 1\n            weights = [rng.randint(1, 2 * m) for _ in range(m)]\n            dec, _ = hamcycle_weighted_decision(g, weights)\n            if dec and hc == 0:\n                fails.append((\"ham_weighted_sound\", gi))\n            C[\"ham_weighted_sound\"] += 1\n            if hc > 0:\n                ham_complete[1] += 1\n                ham_complete[0] += int(dec)\n\n        if (gi + 1) % 200 == 0:\n            log(f\"  {gi + 1}/{len(graphs)} graphs, {len(fails)} failures, {time.time() - t0:.1f} s\")\n\n    res[\"checks\"] = C\n    res[\"ham_weighted_complete\"] = {\"decided_yes\": ham_complete[0], \"with_cycle\": ham_complete[1]}\n    # linear size bounds, as measured constants\n    lin = {}\n    for key, rows in sizes.items():\n        if rows:\n            lin[key] = {\"max_vars_over_n_plus_m\": max(v / (n + m) for n, m, v, c in rows),\n                        \"max_clauses_over_n_plus_m\": max(c / (n + m) for n, m, v, c in rows)}\n    res[\"size_constants\"] = lin\n    res[\"threshold_aux\"] = threshold_aux_ratio()\n    res[\"crossover_table\"] = crossover_table()\n    res[\"seconds\"] = time.time() - t0\n    log(f\"checks: {sum(C.values())} evaluations, {len(fails)} failures, {res['seconds']:.1f} s\")\n    for k, v in C.items():\n        log(f\"  {k}: {v}\")\n    log(f\"Cut & Count weighted decision: yes on {ham_complete[0]} of {ham_complete[1]} graphs with a cycle\"\n        f\" (sound on all: {C['ham_weighted_sound']} checked)\")\n    log(\"size constants: \" + json.dumps(lin))\n    log(f\"threshold auxiliaries per input, n ≤ 200: ≤ {res['threshold_aux']['max_aux_per_input']:.2f}\")\n    log(format_table(res[\"crossover_table\"]))\n    if fails:\n        log(\"FAILURES: \" + str(fails[:20]))\n    (out_dir / \"check.json\").write_text(json.dumps(res, indent=1, default=str))\n    return res\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"--nmax\", type=int, default=7)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--table\", action=\"store_true\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out\", type=Path, default=OUT)\n    a = ap.parse_args()\n    if a.table:\n        print(format_table(crossover_table()))\n        return\n    res = run_checks(a.nmax, a.out)\n    sys.exit(1 if res[\"failures\"] else 0)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JZE7n1Z783LG98tZekueod","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /home/al/dev/MOSP/learning/subexp_crossover.py (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2f64960-c328-4d7b-b5d1-fcb61f9722bb","uuid":"afd189c3-1d25-4455-85c0-52c4f6121c61","timestamp":"2026-11-04T23:05:24.173Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/learning/subexp_crossover.py","content":"\"\"\"Algorithms from the counting theorem for problems on graphs of linear\npathwidth: the encodings of loop0014 item 06 (`reports/subexp_pathwidth.md`\n§6), each checked by brute force on every graph of the networkx atlas (all\ngraphs to 7 vertices) before it was stated, and the crossover table.\n\n    python -m learning.subexp_crossover            # the full check, atlas to 7\n    python -m learning.subexp_crossover --nmax 5   # quick\n    python -m learning.subexp_crossover --table    # the crossover table only\n\nGraphs are `(n, adj)` with `adj` a list of neighbour bitmasks, as in\n`paper1/complex_check.py`. A CNF is a list of clauses, each a list of\nnon-zero ints (DIMACS literals); `count_models` is CaDiCaL with a blocking\nclause over every variable (`learning.subexp_chain`), so it counts exactly.\n\nThe encodings, every one with one Boolean variable per vertex (or per edge)\nand auxiliary variables that are *functions* of those, so that the model\ncount is the count of the combinatorial objects (count-preserving):\n\n- `indep_cnf`: independent sets — `¬x_u ∨ ¬x_w` per edge; width 2, `n`\n  variables, `m` clauses; `count = #independent sets` (ETH paper, Cor. 1.3).\n- `indep_atleast_cnf(g, t)`: independent sets of size `≥ t` — the same plus\n  `Σ x_v ≥ t` compiled through a binary adder tree (`popcount_circuit`) and a\n  comparator against the constant `t` (`ge_const`), Tseitin-encoded, width\n  3, `O(n)` auxiliary variables (`THRESHOLD_AUX_PER_INPUT` measured);\n  satisfiable iff `α(G) ≥ t`, `count = #{S independent : |S| ≥ t}`.\n- `coloring_cnf(g, q)`: proper `q`-colourings — `q n` variables, exactly one\n  colour per vertex (one clause of width `q`, `C(q, 2)` of width 2), no\n  equal colours across an edge (`q` clauses of width 2 per edge);\n  `count = #proper q-colourings` (Cor. 1.3).\n- `domset_cnf(g)`: dominating sets — `x_v ∨ ⋁_{u ∈ N(v)} x_u` per vertex,\n  width `Δ + 1`; `domset_cnf(g, tseitin=True)` compiles each clause to width\n  3 with `deg(v)` auxiliaries, so `n + 2m` variables; `domset_atmost_cnf`\n  adds `Σ x_v ≤ t`; satisfiable iff `γ(G) ≤ t`.\n- `maxcut_cnf(g, t)`: one side bit per vertex, one XOR auxiliary per edge,\n  `Σ_e (x_u ⊕ x_w) ≥ t` through the adder tree; `n + O(m)` variables,\n  width 3; satisfiable iff `maxcut(G) ≥ t`, `count = #{sides : cut ≥ t}`.\n- `hamcycle_cutcount_cnf(g)`: Cut & Count with the DP replaced by a count —\n  one variable per edge, one side bit per vertex, exactly two chosen edges\n  at every vertex (two thresholds), a chosen edge keeps both ends on one\n  side, vertex 0 on side 0; `count = Σ_{2-factors X} 2^{cc(X) − 1}`, so\n  `count ≡ #Hamiltonian cycles (mod 2)`. With the isolation lemma's random\n  edge weights (the weighted count, paper form only) the decision follows;\n  `hamcycle_weighted_decision` is that decision by enumeration.\n\n`crossover_table` tabulates `n / (log₂ c · √ln n)` (the paper exponent with\nconstant 1) and `ρ(n) / log₂ c` (the verified exponent, constant 1) for\n`c = 2, 3, 4`: the pathwidth above which `c^{pw}` exceeds the counting bound.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport itertools\nimport json\nimport math\nimport random\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom learning.subexp_chain import count_models\nfrom learning.subexp_reductions import atlas\n\nOUT = Path(\"reports/scratch/subexp_pathwidth/06_crossover\")\n\n\ndef bits(x: int):\n    while x:\n        b = x & -x\n        yield b.bit_length() - 1\n        x ^= b\n\n\ndef popcount(x: int) -> int:\n    return bin(x).count(\"1\")\n\n\ndef edges_of(g):\n    n, adj = g\n    return [(u, w) for u in range(n) for w in bits(adj[u]) if u < w]\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# a Tseitin circuit builder\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass Builder:\n    \"\"\"Clauses over variables `1..nvars`; `fresh()` allocates. `TRUE` is a\n    variable fixed by a unit clause, so constants are determined too and the\n    count is preserved.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, nvars: int = 0):\n        self.nvars = nvars\n        self.clauses: list[list[int]] = []\n        self._true = None\n\n    def fresh(self) -> int:\n        self.nvars += 1\n        return self.nvars\n\n    @property\n    def TRUE(self) -> int:\n        if self._true is None:\n            self._true = self.fresh()\n            self.clauses.append([self._true])\n        return self._true\n\n    @property\n    def FALSE(self) -> int:\n        return -self.TRUE\n\n    def add(self, clause):\n        self.clauses.append(list(clause))\n\n    def xor(self, a: int, b: int) -> int:\n        z = self.fresh()\n        self.add([-a, -b, -z]); self.add([a, b, -z]); self.add([a, -b, z]); self.add([-a, b, z])\n        return z\n\n    def and_(self, a: int, b: int) -> int:\n        z = self.fresh()\n        self.add([-a, -b, z]); self.add([a, -z]); self.add([b, -z])\n        return z\n\n    def or_(self, a: int, b: int) -> int:\n        z = self.fresh()\n        self.add([a, b, -z]); self.add([-a, z]); self.add([-b, z])\n        return z\n\n    def or_many(self, lits) -> int:\n        \"\"\"OR of a list as a chain of binary ORs: `len − 1` auxiliaries.\"\"\"\n        lits = list(lits)\n        if not lits:\n            return self.FALSE\n        acc = lits[0]\n        for l in lits[1:]:\n            acc = self.or_(acc, l)\n        return acc\n\n    def full_adder(self, a: int, b: int, c: int):\n        t = self.xor(a, b)\n        s = self.xor(t, c)\n        carry = self.or_(self.and_(a, b), self.and_(t, c))\n        return s, carry\n\n    def add_numbers(self, A: list[int], B: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Ripple-carry sum of two little-endian bit lists.\"\"\"\n        L = max(len(A), len(B))\n        out, carry = [], None\n        for i in range(L):\n            a = A[i] if i < len(A) else self.FALSE\n            b = B[i] if i < len(B) else self.FALSE\n            if carry is None:\n                s = self.xor(a, b)\n                carry = self.and_(a, b)\n            else:\n                s, carry = self.full_adder(a, b, carry)\n            out.append(s)\n        out.append(carry)\n        return out\n\n    def popcount_circuit(self, lits) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"The binary adder tree: the number of true literals as a\n        little-endian bit list. Total size `O(len)`: level `j` has `len / 2^j`\n        adders of `j + 1` bits.\"\"\"\n        nums = [[l] for l in lits]\n        if not nums:\n            return [self.FALSE]\n        while len(nums) > 1:\n            nxt = [self.add_numbers(nums[i], nums[i + 1]) for i in range(0, len(nums) - 1, 2)]\n            if len(nums) % 2:\n                nxt.append(nums[-1])\n            nums = nxt\n        return nums[0]\n\n    def ge_const(self, num: list[int], t: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"A literal true iff the little-endian number `num` is `≥ t`.\"\"\"\n        L = max(len(num), t.bit_length())\n        ge = self.TRUE\n        for i in range(L):\n            b = num[i] if i < len(num) else self.FALSE\n            ge = self.and_(b, ge) if (t >> i) & 1 else self.or_(b, ge)\n        return ge\n\n    def at_least(self, lits, t: int) -> None:\n        lits = list(lits)\n        if t <= 0:\n            return\n        self.add([self.ge_const(self.popcount_circuit(lits), t)])\n\n    def at_most(self, lits, t: int) -> None:\n        lits = list(lits)\n        self.at_least([-l for l in lits], len(lits) - t)\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# the encodings\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef indep_cnf(g):\n    n, adj = g\n    return [[-(u + 1), -(w + 1)] for u, w in edges_of(g)], n\n\n\ndef indep_atleast_cnf(g, t: int):\n    n, adj = g\n    b = Builder(n)\n    for c, _ in [indep_cnf(g)]:\n        for cl in c:\n            b.add(cl)\n    b.at_least(range(1, n + 1), t)\n    return b.clauses, b.nvars\n\n\ndef coloring_cnf(g, q: int):\n    n, adj = g\n\n    def x(v, c):\n        return v * q + c + 1\n\n    clauses = []\n    for v in range(n):\n        clauses.append([x(v, c) for c in range(q)])\n        for c1 in range(q):\n            for c2 in range(c1 + 1, q):\n                clauses.append([-x(v, c1), -x(v, c2)])\n    for u, w in edges_of(g):\n        for c in range(q):\n            clauses.append([-x(u, c), -x(w, c)])\n    return clauses, n * q\n\n\ndef domset_cnf(g, tseitin: bool = False):\n    n, adj = g\n    if not tseitin:\n        return [[v + 1] + [u + 1 for u in bits(adj[v])] for v in range(n)], n\n    b = Builder(n)\n    for v in range(n):\n        b.add([b.or_many([v + 1] + [u + 1 for u in bits(adj[v])])])\n    return b.clauses, b.nvars\n\n\ndef domset_atmost_cnf(g, t: int):\n    n, adj = g\n    b = Builder(n)\n    for v in range(n):\n        b.add([b.or_many([v + 1] + [u + 1 for u in bits(adj[v])])])\n    b.at_most(range(1, n + 1), t)\n    return b.clauses, b.nvars\n\n\ndef maxcut_cnf(g, t: int):\n    n, adj = g\n    b = Builder(n)\n    cut = [b.xor(u + 1, w + 1) for u, w in edges_of(g)]\n    b.at_least(cut, t)\n    return b.clauses, b.nvars\n\n\ndef hamcycle_cutcount_cnf(g):\n    \"\"\"Variables `1..m` the edges (in `edges_of` order), `m+1..m+n` the sides.\"\"\"\n    n, adj = g\n    E = edges_of(g)\n    m = len(E)\n    b = Builder(m + n)\n    side = [m + v + 1 for v in range(n)]\n    inc = {v: [] for v in range(n)}\n    for i, (u, w) in enumerate(E):\n        inc[u].append(i + 1)\n        inc[w].append(i + 1)\n    for v in range(n):\n        b.at_least(inc[v], 2)\n        b.at_most(inc[v], 2)\n    for i, (u, w) in enumerate(E):\n        e = i + 1\n        b.add([-e, -side[u], side[w]])\n        b.add([-e, side[u], -side[w]])\n    if n:\n        b.add([-side[0]])\n    return b.clauses, b.nvars\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# ground truth, by enumeration that shares nothing with the encodings\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef independent_sets(g):\n    n, adj = g\n    return [S for S in range(1 << n) if all(adj[v] & S == 0 for v in bits(S))]\n\n\ndef dominating_sets(g):\n    n, adj = g\n    full = (1 << n) - 1\n    out = []\n    for S in range(1 << n):\n        N = S\n        for v in bits(S):\n            N |= adj[v]\n        if N == full:\n            out.append(S)\n    return out\n\n\ndef proper_colorings(g, q: int) -> int:\n    n, adj = g\n    E = edges_of(g)\n    return sum(1 for col in itertools.product(range(q), repeat=n)\n               if all(col[u] != col[w] for u, w in E))\n\n\ndef cut_sizes(g):\n    n, adj = g\n    E = edges_of(g)\n    return [sum(1 for u, w in E if (S >> u) & 1 != (S >> w) & 1) for S in range(1 << n)]\n\n\ndef hamiltonian_cycles(g) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Hamiltonian cycles as edge sets: closed tours from vertex 0, divided\n    by 2 (the two directions).\"\"\"\n    n, adj = g\n    if n < 3:\n        return 0\n    cnt = 0\n    for perm in itertools.permutations(range(1, n)):\n        tour = (0,) + perm\n        if all((adj[tour[i]] >> tour[(i + 1) % n]) & 1 for i in range(n)):\n            cnt += 1\n    return cnt // 2\n\n\ndef two_factors(g):\n    \"\"\"Every 2-regular spanning subgraph as an edge subset, with its number\n    of components. Enumerates edge subsets: for `m ≤ 16` only.\"\"\"\n    n, adj = g\n    E = edges_of(g)\n    m = len(E)\n    out = []\n    for X in range(1 << m):\n        deg = [0] * n\n        for i in bits(X):\n            u, w = E[i]\n            deg[u] += 1\n            deg[w] += 1\n        if any(d != 2 for d in deg):\n            continue\n        # components\n        seen, cc = 0, 0\n        nb = [0] * n\n        for i in bits(X):\n            u, w = E[i]\n            nb[u] |= 1 << w\n            nb[w] |= 1 << u\n        for v in range(n):\n            if (seen >> v) & 1:\n                continue\n            cc += 1\n            stack = [v]\n            seen |= 1 << v\n            while stack:\n                a = stack.pop()\n                for c in bits(nb[a] & ~seen):\n                    seen |= 1 << c\n                    stack.append(c)\n        out.append((X, cc))\n    return out\n\n\ndef hamcycle_weighted_decision(g, weights: list[int], limit: int = 10 ** 6):\n    \"\"\"The Cut & Count decision with the given edge weights, by enumerating\n    the models of `hamcycle_cutcount_cnf`: the coefficient of `y^w` in\n    `Σ_X 2^{cc(X) − 1} y^{w(X)}` for each `w`; the answer is \"yes\" iff some\n    coefficient is odd. Sound always; complete with probability `≥ 1/2` under\n    the isolation lemma's weights (Cygan et al. 2011, Lemma 2.1 / Theorem 1).\n    Returns `(decision, coefficients)`.\"\"\"\n    from pysat.solvers import Solver\n    clauses, nvars = hamcycle_cutcount_cnf(g)\n    m = len(edges_of(g))\n    coef: dict[int, int] = {}\n    cnt = 0\n    with Solver(name=\"cadical195\", bootstrap_with=clauses) as s:\n        while s.solve():\n            cnt += 1\n            if cnt > limit:\n                raise RuntimeError(\"model limit\")\n            model = s.get_model()\n            X = [i for i in range(m) if model[i] > 0]\n            w = sum(weights[i] for i in X)\n            coef[w] = coef.get(w, 0) + 1\n            s.add_clause([-l for l in model[:nvars]])\n    return any(c % 2 for c in coef.values()), coef\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# sizes and the crossover table\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef cnf_size(clauses, nvars: int) -> dict:\n    return {\"variables\": nvars, \"clauses\": len(clauses),\n            \"incidence\": sum(len(c) for c in clauses),\n            \"width\": max((len(c) for c in clauses), default=0)}\n\n\ndef threshold_aux_ratio(nmax: int = 200) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Auxiliary variables of `Σ_{i ≤ n} x_i ≥ t` per input, over all `n ≤ nmax`\n    and `t ∈ {1, ⌈n/2⌉, n}`: the constant in `O(n)`.\"\"\"\n    worst = 0.0\n    rows = {}\n    for n in range(1, nmax + 1):\n        for t in {1, (n + 1) // 2, n}:\n            b = Builder(n)\n            b.at_least(range(1, n + 1), t)\n            aux = b.nvars - n\n            worst = max(worst, aux / n)\n            if n in (1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 200) and t == n:\n                rows[n] = {\"aux\": aux, \"clauses\": len(b.clauses), \"width\": max(len(c) for c in b.clauses)}\n    return {\"max_aux_per_input\": worst, \"rows\": rows}\n\n\ndef rho(n: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"The verified runtime scale `n (log log(n + 16))² / √log(n + 16)`.\"\"\"\n    return n * math.log(math.log(n + 16)) ** 2 / math.sqrt(math.log(n + 16))\n\n\ndef crossover_table(cs=(2, 3, 4), exps=(2, 3, 4, 5, 6)) -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"For each `c` and `n = 10^e`: the pathwidth `pw*` with `c^{pw*} = 2^{E(n)}`,\n    `E` the paper exponent `n / √ln n` and the verified `ρ(n)`, both with\n    constant 1; `pw* = E(n) / log₂ c`; and `pw* / n`.\"\"\"\n    rows = []\n    for c in cs:\n        for e in exps:\n            n = 10 ** e\n            paper = n / math.sqrt(math.log(n))\n            ver = rho(n)\n            rows.append({\"c\": c, \"n\": n,\n                         \"paper_exponent\": paper, \"paper_pw_star\": paper / math.log2(c),\n                         \"paper_ratio\": paper / math.log2(c) / n,\n                         \"verified_exponent\": ver, \"verified_pw_star\": ver / math.log2(c),\n                         \"verified_ratio\": ver / math.log2(c) / n})\n    return rows\n\n\ndef format_table(rows) -> str:\n    lines = [\"| c | n | paper: pw* = n/(log₂c √ln n) | pw*/n | verified: pw* = ρ(n)/log₂c | pw*/n |\",\n             \"|---|---|---|---|---|---|\"]\n    for r in rows:\n        lines.append(f\"| {r['c']} | 10^{int(math.log10(r['n']))} | {r['paper_pw_star']:,.0f} | \"\n                     f\"{r['paper_ratio']:.3f} | {r['verified_pw_star']:,.0f} | {r['verified_ratio']:.3f} |\")\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# the checks\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef run_checks(nmax: int = 7, out_dir: Path = OUT, log=print, qs=(2, 3), q4_nmax: int = 6,\n               twofactor_mmax: int = 15, seed: int = 0) -> dict:\n    out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\n    t0 = time.time()\n    graphs = atlas(nmax)\n    log(f\"atlas to {nmax} vertices: {len(graphs)} graphs\")\n    res = {\"nmax\": nmax, \"graphs\": len(graphs), \"failures\": [], \"checks\": {}}\n    fails = res[\"failures\"]\n    C = {k: 0 for k in [\"indep_count\", \"indep_width\", \"indep_size\",\n                        \"indep_atleast_count\", \"indep_atleast_sat\", \"indep_atleast_width\",\n                        \"coloring_count\", \"coloring_width\", \"coloring_size\",\n                        \"domset_count\", \"domset_width\", \"domset_tseitin_count\", \"domset_tseitin_width\",\n                        \"domset_atmost_sat\", \"maxcut_sat\", \"maxcut_count\", \"maxcut_width\",\n                        \"ham_parity\", \"ham_count_2factors\", \"ham_weighted_sound\", \"ham_width\",\n                        \"ham_size\"]}\n    sizes = {\"indep\": [], \"indep_atleast\": [], \"coloring3\": [], \"domset_tseitin\": [], \"maxcut\": [], \"ham\": []}\n    ham_complete = [0, 0]\n    for gi, g in enumerate(graphs):\n        n, adj = g\n        E = edges_of(g)\n        m = len(E)\n\n        # independent sets\n        cl, nv = indep_cnf(g)\n        IS = independent_sets(g)\n        sz = cnf_size(cl, nv)\n        if count_models(cl, nv) != len(IS):\n            fails.append((\"indep_count\", gi))\n        C[\"indep_count\"] += 1\n        if sz[\"width\"] > 2:\n            fails.append((\"indep_width\", gi))\n        C[\"indep_width\"] += 1\n        if not (nv == n and sz[\"clauses\"] == m):\n            fails.append((\"indep_size\", gi))\n        C[\"indep_size\"] += 1\n        sizes[\"indep\"].append((n, m, nv, sz[\"clauses\"]))\n        alpha = max(popcount(S) for S in IS)\n        for t in range(n + 2):\n            cl, nv = indep_atleast_cnf(g, t)\n            cnt = count_models(cl, nv)\n            if cnt != sum(1 for S in IS if popcount(S) >= t):\n                fails.append((\"indep_atleast_count\", gi, t))\n            C[\"indep_atleast_count\"] += 1\n            if (cnt > 0) != (alpha >= t):\n                fails.append((\"indep_atleast_sat\", gi, t))\n            C[\"indep_atleast_sat\"] += 1\n            sz = cnf_size(cl, nv)\n            if sz[\"width\"] > 3:\n                fails.append((\"indep_atleast_width\", gi, t))\n            C[\"indep_atleast_width\"] += 1\n            if t == (n + 1) // 2:\n                sizes[\"indep_atleast\"].append((n, m, nv, sz[\"clauses\"]))\n\n        # colourings\n        for q in list(qs) + ([4] if n <= q4_nmax else []):\n            cl, nv = coloring_cnf(g, q)\n            if count_models(cl, nv) != proper_colorings(g, q):\n                fails.append((\"coloring_count\", gi, q))\n            C[\"coloring_count\"] += 1\n            sz = cnf_size(cl, nv)\n            if sz[\"width\"] > max(q, 2):\n                fails.append((\"coloring_width\", gi, q))\n            C[\"coloring_width\"] += 1\n            if not (nv == n * q and sz[\"clauses\"] == n + n * q * (q - 1) // 2 + q * m):\n                fails.append((\"coloring_size\", gi, q))\n            C[\"coloring_size\"] += 1\n            if q == 3:\n                sizes[\"coloring3\"].append((n, m, nv, sz[\"clauses\"]))\n\n        # dominating sets\n        DS = dominating_sets(g)\n        gamma = min(popcount(S) for S in DS)\n        Delta = max((popcount(a) for a in adj), default=0)\n        cl, nv = domset_cnf(g)\n        if count_models(cl, nv) != len(DS):\n            fails.append((\"domset_count\", gi))\n        C[\"domset_count\"] += 1\n        if cnf_size(cl, nv)[\"width\"] != Delta + 1:\n            fails.append((\"domset_width\", gi))\n        C[\"domset_width\"] += 1\n        cl, nv = domset_cnf(g, tseitin=True)\n        if count_models(cl, nv) != len(DS):\n            fails.append((\"domset_tseitin_count\", gi))\n        C[\"domset_tseitin_count\"] += 1\n        sz = cnf_size(cl, nv)\n        if sz[\"width\"] > 3 or nv > n + 2 * m + 1:\n            fails.append((\"domset_tseitin_width\", gi))\n        C[\"domset_tseitin_width\"] += 1\n        sizes[\"domset_tseitin\"].append((n, m, nv, sz[\"clauses\"]))\n        for t in range(n + 1):\n            cl, nv = domset_atmost_cnf(g, t)\n            if (count_models(cl, nv) > 0) != (gamma <= t):\n                fails.append((\"domset_atmost_sat\", gi, t))\n            C[\"domset_atmost_sat\"] += 1\n\n        # max cut\n        cuts = cut_sizes(g)\n        mc = max(cuts)\n        for t in range(m + 2):\n            cl, nv = maxcut_cnf(g, t)\n            cnt = count_models(cl, nv)\n            if (cnt > 0) != (mc >= t):\n                fails.append((\"maxcut_sat\", gi, t))\n            C[\"maxcut_sat\"] += 1\n            if cnt != sum(1 for c in cuts if c >= t):\n                fails.append((\"maxcut_count\", gi, t))\n            C[\"maxcut_count\"] += 1\n            sz = cnf_size(cl, nv)\n            if sz[\"width\"] > 3:\n                fails.append((\"maxcut_width\", gi, t))\n            C[\"maxcut_width\"] += 1\n            if t == (m + 1) // 2:\n                sizes[\"maxcut\"].append((n, m, nv, sz[\"clauses\"]))\n\n        # Hamiltonian cycles: Cut & Count as a count\n        if n >= 3:\n            cl, nv = hamcycle_cutcount_cnf(g)\n            cnt = count_models(cl, nv)\n            hc = hamiltonian_cycles(g)\n            if cnt % 2 != hc % 2:\n                fails.append((\"ham_parity\", gi))\n            C[\"ham_parity\"] += 1\n            sz = cnf_size(cl, nv)\n            if sz[\"width\"] > 3:\n                fails.append((\"ham_width\", gi))\n            C[\"ham_width\"] += 1\n            if nv > m + n + 40 * (2 * m) + 1:\n                fails.append((\"ham_size\", gi))\n            C[\"ham_size\"] += 1\n            sizes[\"ham\"].append((n, m, nv, sz[\"clauses\"]))\n            if m <= twofactor_mmax:\n                tf = two_factors(g)\n                if cnt != sum(2 ** (cc - 1) for _, cc in tf):\n                    fails.append((\"ham_count_2factors\", gi))\n                C[\"ham_count_2factors\"] += 1\n            weights = [rng.randint(1, 2 * m) for _ in range(m)]\n            dec, _ = hamcycle_weighted_decision(g, weights)\n            if dec and hc == 0:\n                fails.append((\"ham_weighted_sound\", gi))\n            C[\"ham_weighted_sound\"] += 1\n            if hc > 0:\n                ham_complete[1] += 1\n                ham_complete[0] += int(dec)\n\n        if (gi + 1) % 200 == 0:\n            log(f\"  {gi + 1}/{len(graphs)} graphs, {len(fails)} failures, {time.time() - t0:.1f} s\")\n\n    res[\"checks\"] = C\n    res[\"ham_weighted_complete\"] = {\"decided_yes\": ham_complete[0], \"with_cycle\": ham_complete[1]}\n    # linear size bounds, as measured constants\n    lin = {}\n    for key, rows in sizes.items():\n        if rows:\n            lin[key] = {\"max_vars_over_n_plus_m\": max(v / (n + m) for n, m, v, c in rows),\n                        \"max_clauses_over_n_plus_m\": max(c / (n + m) for n, m, v, c in rows)}\n    res[\"size_constants\"] = lin\n    res[\"threshold_aux\"] = threshold_aux_ratio()\n    res[\"crossover_table\"] = crossover_table()\n    res[\"seconds\"] = time.time() - t0\n    log(f\"checks: {sum(C.values())} evaluations, {len(fails)} failures, {res['seconds']:.1f} s\")\n    for k, v in C.items():\n        log(f\"  {k}: {v}\")\n    log(f\"Cut & Count weighted decision: yes on {ham_complete[0]} of {ham_complete[1]} graphs with a cycle\"\n        f\" (sound on all: {C['ham_weighted_sound']} checked)\")\n    log(\"size constants: \" + json.dumps(lin))\n    log(f\"threshold auxiliaries per input, n ≤ 200: ≤ {res['threshold_aux']['max_aux_per_input']:.2f}\")\n    log(format_table(res[\"crossover_table\"]))\n    if fails:\n        log(\"FAILURES: \" + str(fails[:20]))\n    (out_dir / \"check.json\").write_text(json.dumps(res, indent=1, default=str))\n    return res\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"--nmax\", type=int, default=7)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--table\", action=\"store_true\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out\", type=Path, default=OUT)\n    a = ap.parse_args()\n    if a.table:\n        print(format_table(crossover_table()))\n        return\n    res = run_checks(a.nmax, a.out)\n    sys.exit(1 if res[\"failures\"] else 0)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JZE7n1Z783LG98tZekueod","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
