{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0133NhxQYM6exQZ1YF63TzJ6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/-\n2\tCopyright (c) 2026 Alexandre Linhares. All rights reserved.\n3\tReleased under the MIT license as described in the file LICENSE.\n4\t\n5\t# The crossover: counting beats the width dynamic programs at linear pathwidth\n6\t\n7\tItem 06 of loop0014 (`reports/subexp_pathwidth.md` §6). Two things, both over the frame of\n8\t`Frame.lean`:\n9\t\n10\t1. **The independent-set algorithm, as a consequence of the counting hypothesis.** `indepCNF G`\n11\t   is the formula of the ETH paper's Corollary 1.3: one Boolean variable per vertex and the clause\n12\t   `¬x_u ∨ ¬x_w` per edge. `indepCNF_width` (width `≤ 2`), `indepCNF_eval_iff` (its models are\n13\t   the independent sets) and `count_indepCNF` (`SAT.count (indepCNF G) = indepCount G`, the number\n14\t   of independent sets) are the encoding's correctness; `indepCount_subexp` is the algorithm:\n15\t   under `SubexpCount 2`, one primitive machine writes the number of independent sets of every\n16\t   graph `G` on `n` vertices on its count tape, on the input `encodeCNF (indepCNF G)`, within\n17\t   `C (L + 1)^d · 2^(A · ρ(n))` steps, `L` the formula's bit length — and the exponent\n18\t   `A · ρ(n)` is `o(n)` in the number of vertices (`isSubexpExponent_runtimeScale`). Nothing is\n19\t   asserted: the theorem is `SubexpCount 2 → …`.\n20\t\n21\t2. **The crossover inequality.** `crossoverThreshold A c n = A ρ(n) / log₂ c` is the pathwidth at\n22\t   which the decomposition dynamic program's `c^pw` equals the counting bound's `2^(A ρ(n))`:\n23\t   `rpow_le_of_crossover` (`pw ≥` threshold `→ 2^(A ρ(n)) ≤ c^pw`), `crossoverThreshold_eventually_lt`\n24\t   (for every `β > 0` the threshold is below `β n` for all large `n`, from `ρ = o(n)`), and\n25\t   `counting_beats_dp_eventually`: on every class of linear pathwidth (`pw G ≥ β n`) the counting\n26\t   bound's exponential factor is at most `c^{pw G}` for all large `n`, for every base `c > 1` and\n27\t   every constant `A`. The polynomial factors and the constants are outside the statement, as\n28\t   they are in the paper.\n29\t\n30\tEvery statement here was brute-force checked before it was stated: the formula's count against\n31\tsubset enumeration on every graph of the atlas to 7 vertices\n32\t(`learning/subexp_crossover.py`, `reports/scratch/subexp_pathwidth/06_crossover/`).\n33\t\n34\tWhat this file does **not** claim: that `SubexpCount 2` holds; that maximum independent set (the\n35\tthreshold `|S| ≥ t`, which needs the adder-tree circuit of §6.2) is formalised — only the count\n36\tis; that any polynomial factor is bounded; that the crossover says anything at a specific `n`\n37\t(the constants `A`, and the paper's, are unknown).\n38\t-/\n39\timport MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.Frame\n40\timport Mathlib.Combinatorics.SimpleGraph.Clique\n41\t\n42\tset_option linter.unusedSectionVars false\n43\t\n44\tnamespace MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth\n45\t\n46\topen OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT\n47\topen OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Computation\n48\topen OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLogSpace\n49\topen OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLog.Statement\n50\topen Asymptotics Filter\n51\t\n52\t/-! ### The independent-set formula -/\n53\t\n54\t/-- The clause `¬x_u ∨ ¬x_w`. -/\n55\tdef edgeClause {n : ℕ} (u w : Fin n) : SAT.Clause (Fin n) :=\n56\t  {⟨u, false⟩, ⟨w, false⟩}\n57\t\n58\t/-- Corollary 1.3's formula: one variable per vertex, `¬x_u ∨ ¬x_w` for every edge. -/\n59\tnoncomputable def indepCNF {n : ℕ} (G : SimpleGraph (Fin n)) : SAT.CNF (Fin n) :=\n60\t  open Classical in\n61\t  (Finset.univ.filter (fun p : Fin n × Fin n => G.Adj p.1 p.2)).image\n62\t    (fun p => edgeClause p.1 p.2)\n63\t\n64\t/-- The number of independent sets of `G`. -/\n65\tnoncomputable def indepCount {n : ℕ} (G : SimpleGraph (Fin n)) : ℕ :=\n66\t  open Classical in\n67\t  (Finset.univ.filter (fun S : Finset (Fin n) => G.IsIndepSet (↑S : Set (Fin n)))).card\n68\t\n69\ttheorem edgeClause_card_le {n : ℕ} (u w : Fin n) : (edgeClause u w).card ≤ 2 :=\n70\t  Finset.card_le_two\n71\t\n72\t/-- The formula has width `≤ 2`. -/\n73\ttheorem indepCNF_width {n : ℕ} (G : SimpleGraph (Fin n)) : SAT.WidthAtMost 2 (indepCNF G) := by\n74\t  intro C hC\n75\t  classical\n76\t  simp only [indepCNF, Finset.mem_image, Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_univ, true_and] at hC\n77\t  obtain ⟨p, -, rfl⟩ := hC\n78\t  exact edgeClause_card_le _ _\n79\t\n80\ttheorem edgeClause_eval {n : ℕ} (a : SAT.Assignment (Fin n)) (u w : Fin n) :\n81\t    (edgeClause u w).eval a = true ↔ (a u = false ∨ a w = false) := by\n82\t  simp [edgeClause, SAT.Clause.eval, SAT.Literal.eval]\n83\t\n84\t/-- A model of `indepCNF G` is an independent set: the vertices set to `true`. -/\n85\ttheorem indepCNF_eval_iff {n : ℕ} (G : SimpleGraph (Fin n)) (a : SAT.Assignment (Fin n)) :\n86\t    (indepCNF G).eval a = true ↔ G.IsIndepSet {v | a v = true} := by\n87\t  classical\n88\t  simp only [SAT.CNF.eval, decide_eq_true_eq, indepCNF, Finset.mem_image, Finset.mem_filter,\n89\t    Finset.mem_univ, true_and, forall_exists_index, and_imp]\n90\t  constructor\n91\t  · intro h v hv w hw hvw hadj\n92\t    have := h _ (v, w) hadj rfl\n93\t    rw [edgeClause_eval] at this\n94\t    simp only [Set.mem_ofPred_eq] at hv hw\n95\t    rcases this with h1 | h1 <;> simp_all\n96\t  · intro hI C p hadj rfl\n97\t    rw [edgeClause_eval]\n98\t    by_cases hu : a p.1 = false\n99\t    · exact Or.inl hu\n100\t    · right\n101\t      by_contra hw\n102\t      have hu' : a p.1 = true := by simpa using hu\n103\t      have hw' : a p.2 = true := by simpa using hw\n104\t      exact hI (by simpa using hu') (by simpa using hw') (G.ne_of_adj hadj) hadj\n105\t\n106\t/-- The model count is the number of independent sets. -/\n107\ttheorem count_indepCNF {n : ℕ} (G : SimpleGraph (Fin n)) :\n108\t    SAT.count (indepCNF G) = indepCount G := by\n109\t  classical\n110\t  unfold SAT.count SAT.satisfyingAssignments indepCount\n111\t  refine Finset.card_nbij' (fun a => Finset.univ.filter (fun v => a v = true))\n112\t    (fun S => fun v => decide (v ∈ S)) ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_\n113\t  · intro a ha\n114\t    simp only [Finset.mem_coe, Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_univ, true_and] at ha ⊢\n115\t    rw [indepCNF_eval_iff] at ha\n116\t    convert ha using 1\n117\t    ext v\n118\t    simp\n119\t  · intro S hS\n120\t    simp only [Finset.mem_coe, Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_univ, true_and] at hS ⊢\n121\t    rw [indepCNF_eval_iff]\n122\t    convert hS using 1\n123\t    ext v\n124\t    simp\n125\t  · intro a _\n126\t    funext v\n127\t    by_cases h : a v = true <;> simp [h]\n128\t  · intro S _\n129\t    ext v\n130\t    simp\n131\t\n132\t/-! ### The algorithm: counting independent sets under the hypothesis -/\n133\t\n134\t/-- **Independent sets are counted in `2^{o(n)} · poly` under the counting hypothesis.** Under\n135\t`SubexpCount 2`, one primitive machine, on the canonical encoding of `indepCNF G`, halts with the\n136\tnumber of independent sets of `G` on its count tape and `decide (0 < indepCount G)` as its\n137\tanswer, within `C (L + 1)^d · 2^(A · ρ(n))` steps, where `L` is the formula's bit length and `n`\n138\tthe number of vertices; `A · ρ(n)` is a subexponential exponent. This is Corollary 1.3's first\n139\tsentence as a consequence of the comparator statement. -/\n140\ttheorem indepCount_subexp (h : SubexpCount 2) :\n141\t    ∃ (machine : PrimitiveMachine) (countTape : Fin machine.tapeCount) (C A : ℝ) (d : ℕ),\n142\t      0 < C ∧ 0 < A ∧ 0 < d ∧ IsSubexpExponent (fun n : ℕ => A * runtimeScale n) ∧\n143\t      ∀ (n : ℕ) (G : SimpleGraph (Fin n)),\n144\t        ∃ (time : ℕ) (final : machine.Cfg),\n145\t          Trace machine.step time (machine.init (Encoding.encodeCNF (indepCNF G))) final ∧\n146\t          final.tapes countTape = Turing.Tape.mk₁ ((countWord (indepCount G)).map some) ∧\n147\t          final.state = Sum.inl (decide (0 < indepCount G)) ∧\n148\t          (time : ℝ) ≤ C * ((Encoding.formulaBitLength (indepCNF G) : ℝ) + 1) ^ d *\n149\t            (2 : ℝ) ^ (A * runtimeScale n) := by\n150\t  obtain ⟨machine, countTape, answerTape, C, A, S, d, e, hC, hA, hS, hd, he, hmain⟩ := h\n151\t  refine ⟨machine, countTape, C, A, d, hC, hA, hd, isSubexpExponent_runtimeScale A, ?_⟩\n152\t  intro n G\n153\t  obtain ⟨time, final, htrace, hcount, -, hstate, -, -, htime, -⟩ :=\n154\t    hmain n (indepCNF G) (indepCNF_width G)\n155\t  refine ⟨time, final.config, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩\n156\t  · have := Trace.config_of_locatedStep htrace\n157\t    simpa [locatedInit] using this\n158\t  · rw [hcount, count_indepCNF]\n159\t  · rw [hstate, count_indepCNF]\n160\t  · simpa [runtimeBound_eq] using htime\n161\t\n162\t/-! ### The crossover inequality -/\n163\t\n164\t/-- The pathwidth at which `c^pw = 2^(A ρ(n))`: above it the counting bound's exponential factor\n165\tis below the decomposition dynamic program's. -/\n166\tnoncomputable def crossoverThreshold (A c : ℝ) (n : ℕ) : ℝ :=\n167\t  A * runtimeScale n / Real.logb 2 c\n168\t\n169\t/-- Above the threshold, `2^(A ρ(n)) ≤ c^pw`. -/\n170\ttheorem rpow_le_of_crossover {A c : ℝ} (hc : 1 < c) {n : ℕ} {pw : ℝ}\n171\t    (h : crossoverThreshold A c n ≤ pw) :\n172\t    (2 : ℝ) ^ (A * runtimeScale n) ≤ c ^ pw := by\n173\t  have hlog : 0 < Real.logb 2 c := Real.logb_pos (by norm_num) hc\n174\t  have hle : A * runtimeScale n ≤ Real.logb 2 c * pw := by\n175\t    rw [crossoverThreshold, div_le_iff₀ hlog] at h\n176\t    linarith\n177\t  calc (2 : ℝ) ^ (A * runtimeScale n)\n178\t      ≤ (2 : ℝ) ^ (Real.logb 2 c * pw) :=\n179\t        Real.rpow_le_rpow_of_exponent_le (by norm_num) hle\n180\t    _ = ((2 : ℝ) ^ Real.logb 2 c) ^ pw := Real.rpow_mul (by norm_num) _ _\n181\t    _ = c ^ pw := by\n182\t        rw [Real.rpow_logb (by norm_num) (by norm_num) (by linarith)]\n183\t\n184\t/-- The threshold is `o(n)`: for every `β > 0` it is below `β n` for all large `n`. -/\n185\ttheorem crossoverThreshold_eventually_lt {A c β : ℝ} (hc : 1 < c) (hβ : 0 < β) :\n186\t    ∀ᶠ n : ℕ in atTop, crossoverThreshold A c n < β * n := by\n187\t  have hlog : 0 < Real.logb 2 c := Real.logb_pos (by norm_num) hc\n188\t  have hlit : (fun n : ℕ => A / Real.logb 2 c * runtimeScale n) =o[atTop]\n189\t      (fun n : ℕ => (n : ℝ)) :=\n190\t    runtimeScale_isLittleO.const_mul_left (A / Real.logb 2 c)\n191\t  have hev := hlit.def (half_pos hβ)\n192\t  filter_upwards [hev, eventually_ge_atTop 1] with n hn hn1\n193\t  have hn' : (1 : ℝ) ≤ n := by exact_mod_cast hn1\n194\t  have hβn : 0 < β * n := by positivity\n195\t  calc crossoverThreshold A c n = A / Real.logb 2 c * runtimeScale n := by\n196\t        unfold crossoverThreshold; ring\n197\t    _ ≤ ‖A / Real.logb 2 c * runtimeScale n‖ := Real.le_norm_self _\n198\t    _ ≤ β / 2 * ‖(n : ℝ)‖ := hn\n199\t    _ = β / 2 * n := by rw [Real.norm_eq_abs, abs_of_nonneg (by positivity)]\n200\t    _ < β * n := by linarith\n201\t\n202\t/-- **The crossover.** On graphs of linear pathwidth (`pw G ≥ β n`), for every base `c > 1` and\n203\tevery constant `A`, the counting bound's exponential factor `2^(A ρ(n))` is at most the\n204\tdecomposition dynamic program's `c^{pw G}` for all large `n`. -/\n205\ttheorem counting_beats_dp_eventually {A c β : ℝ} (hc : 1 < c) (hβ : 0 < β) :\n206\t    ∀ᶠ n : ℕ in atTop, ∀ G : SimpleGraph (Fin n),\n207\t      β * n ≤ (pathwidth G : ℝ) → (2 : ℝ) ^ (A * runtimeScale n) ≤ c ^ (pathwidth G : ℝ) := by\n208\t  filter_upwards [crossoverThreshold_eventually_lt (A := A) hc hβ] with n hn G hG\n209\t  exact rpow_le_of_crossover hc (le_trans hn.le hG)\n210\t\n211\tend MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth\n212\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011qJdkAuUyVw9TukvPsbhHk","agent_id":"aea14e2d2e4e48aa4","session_id":"e2f64960-c328-4d7b-b5d1-fcb61f9722bb","uuid":"9d96c4df-3252-43a1-824a-ac115d394198","timestamp":"2026-11-04T23:10:34.655Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0133NhxQYM6exQZ1YF63TzJ6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source"