{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GWM2XFWEpthsqEH9rUfMXs","type":"tool_result","content":"9:## 0. Summary\n14:## 1. The audit and the kill check (item 01, 2026-11-04)\n16:### 1.0 What was read, and how\n65:### 1.1 (a) The best published exact algorithms, with their bases\n103:### 1.2 (b) ETH- and SETH-conditional lower bounds on computing these parameters\n168:### 1.3 (c) What the counting method needs from a problem — in our words\n341:### 1.4 The kill check (plan §0.6)\n371:### 1.5 What this does not claim\n391:### 1.6 Regenerate\n399:## 2. The formal frame: `SubexpCount`, `PathwidthSubexp`, `PathwidthSubexpOn` (item 02, 2026-11-04)\n408:### 2.1 The decision: the machine model is copied verbatim\n466:### 2.2 The hypothesis, exactly\n498:### 2.3 The target, in the same model\n565:### 2.4 Glue between the two: the verified bound has the target's shape\n589:### 2.5 What a transfer theorem will look like, given this frame\n617:### 2.6 Checks\n641:### 2.7 What this does not claim\n661:### 2.8 Regenerate\n668:## 3. The reduction catalogue: every reduction into pathwidth or vertex separation on record, with its blow-up (item 03, 2026-11-04)\n682:### 3.0 What was read, and how\n715:### 3.1 The catalogue\n748:### 3.2 The best `X` with a linear reduction\n798:### 3.3 What the superlinear reductions lose, and where\n822:### 3.4 The three linear constructions, with proofs\n923:### 3.5 The checks\n955:### 3.6 What this does not claim\n980:### 3.7 Regenerate\n988:## 4. Classes with `O(n)`-bit layouts? Cobipartite, split, maximum degree 3, cocomparability, the clique-tree covers (item 04, 2026-11-04)\n1004:### 4.0 What \"fits\" means here\n1031:### 4.1 Cobipartite graphs: one clique first, then a chain on the other side\n1126:### 4.2 Split graphs: polynomial, so the question is moot — and a two-vertex certificate\n1178:### 4.3 Graphs of maximum degree 3: the orientation is not a certificate\n1220:### 4.4 Cocomparability and AT-free graphs: the same question as the general case\n1237:### 4.5 Chordal graphs, starlike graphs and the clique-tree covers of paper 2: twins, units and a `2^{O(√n)}` subclass\n1344:### 4.6 The gap lemma: no certificate that carries the chain up to local permutations fits\n1434:### 4.7 Verdict: no NP-hard class fits; the positive track is the chain-count attempt only\n1464:### 4.8 The checks\n1489:### 4.9 What this does not claim\n1533:### 4.10 Regenerate\n1540:## 5. The chain count as an algebraic object (item 05, 2026-11-04)\n1422:and put the crossover near `10⁹`; the refuter caught the mix.) The\n1443:| any chain-carrying certificate at spacing `g` | — | `N ≥ n log₂(n/(eg)) − 1` (Lemma 4.6) | **no** on the verified route at every `n ≥ 16`; on the paper route asymptotically (crossover beyond `10²⁴`) |\n====\n\"\"\"loop0014 item 06: the encodings of `reports/subexp_pathwidth.md` §6 against\nbrute force on small graphs (the full atlas run is\n`python -m learning.subexp_crossover`).\"\"\"\nimport math\nimport random\n\nfrom learning import subexp_crossover as sx\nfrom learning.subexp_reductions import atlas\nfrom paper1.complex_check import graph\n\n\ndef _graphs(nmax):\n    return atlas(nmax)\n\n\ndef test_indep_cnf_counts_independent_sets_and_has_width_two():\n    for g in _graphs(5):\n        cl, nv = sx.indep_cnf(g)\n        assert sx.count_models(cl, nv) == len(sx.independent_sets(g))\n        assert sx.cnf_size(cl, nv)[\"width\"] <= 2\n        assert nv == g[0]\n\n\ndef test_indep_atleast_is_count_preserving_and_decides_alpha():\n    for g in _graphs(5):\n        IS = sx.independent_sets(g)\n        alpha = max(sx.popcount(S) for S in IS)\n        for t in range(g[0] + 2):\n            cl, nv = sx.indep_atleast_cnf(g, t)\n            cnt = sx.count_models(cl, nv)\n            assert cnt == sum(1 for S in IS if sx.popcount(S) >= t)\n            assert (cnt > 0) == (alpha >= t)\n            assert sx.cnf_size(cl, nv)[\"width\"] <= 3\n\n\ndef test_threshold_circuit_is_linear():\n    r = sx.threshold_aux_ratio(120)\n    assert r[\"max_aux_per_input\"] <= 7.0\n    assert all(row[\"width\"] <= 3 for row in r[\"rows\"].values())\n\n\ndef test_coloring_cnf_counts_proper_colorings():\n    for g in _graphs(5):\n        for q in (2, 3):\n            cl, nv = sx.coloring_cnf(g, q)\n            assert sx.count_models(cl, nv) == sx.proper_colorings(g, q)\n            assert nv == q * g[0]\n            assert sx.cnf_size(cl, nv)[\"width\"] <= max(q, 2)\n\n\ndef test_domset_cnfs_count_dominating_sets_and_decide_gamma():\n    for g in _graphs(5):\n        DS = sx.dominating_sets(g)\n        gamma = min(sx.popcount(S) for S in DS)\n        for ts in (False, True):\n            cl, nv = sx.domset_cnf(g, tseitin=ts)\n            assert sx.count_models(cl, nv) == len(DS)\n        for t in range(g[0] + 1):\n            cl, nv = sx.domset_atmost_cnf(g, t)\n            assert (sx.count_models(cl, nv) > 0) == (gamma <= t)\n3.3","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011qJdkAuUyVw9TukvPsbhHk","agent_id":"aea14e2d2e4e48aa4","session_id":"e2f64960-c328-4d7b-b5d1-fcb61f9722bb","uuid":"4f6a2db4-b1ce-455d-a64f-a1069306e4dc","timestamp":"2026-11-04T23:15:24.757Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GWM2XFWEpthsqEH9rUfMXs","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Refute item 06's statements"}
