{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015i8KezQ3kENP8A1EY2SiLE","type":"tool_result","content":"| 10⁹ | 0.50 | 0.26 | 4.55 | 0.016 | 9.4 × 10⁷ | 4.92 × 10⁸ | 0.19 |\n| 10¹⁵ | 0.47 | 0.27 | 5.88 | 0.006 | 4.6 × 10¹³ | 1.56 × 10¹⁴ | 0.29 |\n| 10²¹ | 0.46 | 0.27 | 6.95 | 0.003 | 2.5 × 10¹⁹ | 4.6 × 10¹⁹ | 0.55 |\n| 10²⁴ | 0.46 | 0.27 | 7.43 | 0.002 | 1.9 × 10²² | 2.4 × 10²² | 0.78 |\n\nSo the paper route is excluded for this family **asymptotically only**:\nthe ratio is below 1 at every `n` up to `10²⁴` and passes it beyond,\nso at any size one could write down the arithmetic alone does not\nexclude a coarse chain on the paper route — with the caveat that\nTheorem D.1's constants are unknown (§1.3.8), so nothing is claimed at\nany finite `n` in either direction. (The first draft mixed the routes,\ntaking `g` from the verified budget and the width against `s = B_p`,\nand put the crossover near `10⁹`; the refuter caught the mix.) The\nverified budget `B_v` is itself below `n` at every `n` in the table,\nwhich is the same fact: the verified exponent is `o(n)` only in the\nlimit.\n\n**What the lemma does not cover.** A certificate that is not a coarse\nchain at all — one whose satisfying assignments do not determine any\ncheckpoint of any layout — is untouched. That is the only kind item 05\ncan look for: an algebraic object (the number of chains as a sum over\n====\n45:  verified statement is the weaker one, `ρ(n) = n (log log n)² / √log n`\n46:  (the paper's Proposition 6.4); the sharper `n log log n / √log n` and the\n47:  fixed-density `n / √log n` of Theorem 1.1 are proved on paper only\n221:  reaches this by branching on the `≤ n/√log n` most frequent variables\n222:  (2176–2192, \"at most `2^{n/√λ}` branches\"), which costs exactly the\n226:  partitions the variables into `r = Θ(√log n / (log log n)²)` groups of\n243:**1.3.4 Where `2^{n/√log n}` comes from.** Three costs multiply (2.11,\n247:the choice `r = Θ(√log n / (log log n)²)`, `Q = Θ(log n / log log n)`,\n248:`R = Θ(√log n)`, `τ = 1/(r log n)`, `D = r^{2Q} ≤ (2n)^{1/128}` (2.10,\n249:641–648; 4.17, 1930–1940) all three are `O(n (log log n)² / √log n)`\n252:`2n/r = Θ(n (log log n)² / √log n)` variables, and the price of making the\n256:`R = Θ(√log n)` and `Q = Θ(log n)` up to log-log factors, and why the gain\n257:is `√log n` and not more. The sharper Appendix D bound replaces the single\n282:constraints must be `O(n)` for a `2^{O(n/√log n)}`-type bound, and\n283:`o(n √log n)` for any `2^{o(n)}` bound at all.**\n323:    N = o(n √log n / (log log n)²)   (verified route)   or   s = o(n √log n)   (paper route),\n332:by a factor `(log log n)² · √log n`** — not a proof of absence, since the\n338:local constraints\": **total incidence `o(n √log n)`, with constraints of\n354:  existence-preserving encoding of total incidence `o(n √log n)` in the\n367:incidence `o(n √log n)` on an NP-hard class, with constraint width free;","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011qJdkAuUyVw9TukvPsbhHk","agent_id":"aea14e2d2e4e48aa4","session_id":"e2f64960-c328-4d7b-b5d1-fcb61f9722bb","uuid":"e6d93c8e-ab2d-4ebd-9f92-a0d020c6fae3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T23:15:29.837Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015i8KezQ3kENP8A1EY2SiLE","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Refute item 06's statements"}
