 at n=50), peaks at 16/e² = 2.165 near n ≈ 10^{23.7}, and crosses 1 again at ln(n+16) ≈ 5504, i.e. n ≈ e^{5504}. The consequence (verified-form c=2 crossover beyond every table n) holds.\\n\\n**GAP**\\n3. The crossover table uses `n` = vertex count, but the exponent is in the *variable* count, which is `n` only for #IS. With the table's own constant-1 convention, maximum independent set (≈8n variables), Max-Cut (≈13n at m=n) and Hamiltonian cycle (≈33n) have **no crossover at any n in the table** (pw*/n = 3.1, 4.8, ≈6 at n=10²; 2.0, 3.2, ≈4 at 10⁶); 3-/4-colouring go from 0.29/0.23 to 0.79/0.82.\\n4. \\\"Paper form n/√ln n\\\" is Theorem 1.1's *fixed-density* bound; for `indepCNF` on dense graphs the applicable one carries an extra log log n.\\n5. The Hamiltonian-cycle *decision* needs the weighted count in Q[y]/(y^ℓ), which `SubexpCount` does not provide and plain counting cannot simulate within budget (a weighted adder is Θ(m log m) gates); it rests on one sentence of eth.txt §3.1 plus Prop. 3.4, unverified here and uncovered by Lean. The parity result and the isolation-lemma arithmetic are right.\\n\\n**OK** (with evidence)\\n- `indepCount_subexp` says exactly what its docstring says (`#check` on the built olean; n is the vertex count; axioms standard; not vacuous/circular). `IsSubexpExponent` is the right notion; `counting_beats_dp_eventually` is trivial and holds for any real ≥ βn (I proved the variant in a scratch file) — editorial suggestions: state the combined time bound with the A of `indepCount_subexp`, note the DP is not modelled, note L = Θ(mn) from unary `encodeNat`.\\n- My own brute force to 6 vertices (209 graphs, own enumerators): 0 failures on #IS, the threshold formula (88,744 fixed-input extension checks, exactly-one-extension form), 3-colouring, Max-Cut (to 5), and Cut & Count (auxiliaries are functions, every model is a 2-factor with consistent sides, total = Σ 2^{cc−1}, parity = own HC count, cc=1 ⇔ HC; weighted decision sound in 615 trials, odd coefficient at every unique minimum).\\n- Paper proofs (b)(i)–(iv) correct; dominating set's direct form needs `SubexpCount (Δ+1)` so bounded degree only; (iii)/(iv) are 2^{o(n)} only at m = O(n).\\n- Framing (d) is right, with a required qualification: eth.txt line 187 says the theorem refutes SETH outright, so the SETH-conditional bounds' *premise* is gone; their conclusions are not contradicted and now rest only on the unrestricted-CNF-SAT hypothesis (or Lampis's pw-SETH); the DP+counting combination gives min(2^{pw}, 2^{o(n)}), never (2−ε)^{pw}.\\n\\n**EDITORIAL**: README (110,307 evaluations, 27 s, no oct) is stale against the new log (129,761, 119 s, oct checks); check.json predates the oct addition; `THRESHOLD_AUX_PER_INPUT` named in the docstring does not exist.\",\"usage\":{\"total_tokens\":161533,\"tool_uses\":19,\"duration_ms\":636539},\"uuid\":\"b4495ee3-543e-4c3f-be08-34623316ce26\",\"session_id\":\"e2f64960-c328-4d7b-b5d1-fcb61f9722bb\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"background_tasks_changed\",\"tasks\":[{\"task_id\":\"byt8zwqn2\",\"run_id\":\"0mw2qmzga-f3a3bbf4\",\"task_type\":\"local_bash\",\"description\":\"Run the loop gate in the background\"}],\"uuid\":\"4b6fa303-6c2d-4d1f-869c-225f5ac75270\",\"session_id\":\"e2f64960-c328-4d7b-b5d1-fcb61f9722bb\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-fable-5-1\",\"id\":\"msg_011CgikBbUT6B61RfuEEN3Rp\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01W8rk5c4sLn8rtiFTYp7J2g\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"cd /tmp/sx06 && python3 - <<'EOF'\\np='/tmp/sx06/Coloring.lean'\\ns=open(p).read()\\ns=s.replace(\\\"end MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth\\\", '''/-! ### The algorithm: counting `q`-colourings under the hypothesis -/\\n\\nopen Asymptotics Filter in\\n/-- `ρ(n q) = o(n)` at fixed `q`: a `q n`-variable encoding keeps the exponent subexponential\\nin the number of vertices. -/\\ntheorem runtimeScale_mul_isLittleO (q : ℕ) :